{"id":"mcp-mirror-op","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"a6","title":"The ops layer cannot place a mirror","done":"2026-08-11T22:13:42-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #117** (squash 7866e08), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T02:13:25Z under the overnight pre-approval — the second fully autonomous merge.\n- **Gate record:** Grok review (six findings, all taken — teaching referenced-retire refusals, Now enumerable via placed/mirrors reads, query tests, master sync)\n- odu 20/20 both platforms at 4d0dd84, CLEAN, roadmap zero-diff\n- Evidence transcript spot-checked by the orchestrator (containment-cycle refusal naming the loop; did-you-mean; placement-retire leaving the target byte-identical)\n- add_mirror / remove_mirror / set_after ship on both faces; ops are LEDGER-COMPLETE — the orchestrator's scripted-edit era ends when its MCP server reconnects onto this build\n\n**Dispatched 2026-08-11** (overnight slate) -> Kolu terminal `1bb73fb1` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `11d79c7f`)\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-node-context","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"a2","title":"Ask the agent about this node: selection becomes chat context","done":"2026-08-13T14:19:23-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11. **Shipped as PR #141 (squash 80e4d65), 2026-08-13.**\n\n**Direction one — arm from a row:**\n- A row's ••• \"Ask agent\" arms the composer with the shown node (a mirror arms what it is a placement of) and opens the panel\n- On the wire the context is ids only, resolved server-side through the same `Query.foundOf` that answers `read_node`, so a context line and a tool call cannot disagree\n- The agent gets one line under the message — a handle it can act on via MCP, never a copy\n\n**Direction two — transcripts point at rows:**\n- Chips on the sent message\n- The node an olai write was about (`Applied.id` finally crosses the wire)\n- Ids the agent writes in backticks become pressable exactly when the loaded set declares them — marked with the RESOLVED id, so a placement id in prose lands on the node it shows\n- Pressing focuses in place when the node is on the page (the address stays put — pinned in e2e) and navigates when it isn't\n- An armed node that has gone refuses the send in ops' own notFound words and the composer restores\n\n**Pipeline:**\n- Grok review found two MUST-FIX (focus-in-place had no pin — always-navigate kept e2e green; placement ids marked with the wrong id), both fixed red-first\n- All six NICE-TO-HAVEs taken including the gone-node join scenario and the palette's > sending armed context\n- Reviewer endorsed keeping see/after links as links (\"an href is a promise about leaving\")\n- Then #140 landed in packages/chat first: master merged, conflicts resolved preserving both features (384/384 e2e together), two-layer delta-verify DELTA-OK\n- CI 10/10 at b4c72a2 on kolu-ci-1\n- The prototype artifact was unfetchable; interaction built from olai's own idioms instead\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"form-elicitation","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"a3","title":"Form elicitation: the agent's questions render as forms","done":"2026-08-11T20:26:45-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #110** (squash 4a7ad66; merged 2026-08-12T00:26:28Z after the human lifted his hold; this done stamp is the ops instant minutes after).\n- The agent's questions render as answerable forms in the chat (AskUserQuestion works over ACP)\n- A refused answer keeps the typed draft\n- Plan mode reaches the human instead of silent auto-approval\n- Review: approve-with-fixes, all findings addressed; 18/18 required checks green both platforms at 9054de8\n\n- All five scope items delivered, verified against the actually-pinned adapter 0.66.0\n- **Scope-5 tightened:** auto-approval is POSITIVE RECOGNITION of session-handed MCP servers; everything else fails toward asking\n- **Carried forward:** the silent-errors cancel-path collision, on that branch's side\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** on the human's decision (\"We want that\") -> Kolu terminal `5931d974` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `47b4e8c9`).\n- **Origin:** the adapter presents AskUserQuestion as an ACP form elicitation when the client advertises elicitation.form and disables the tool otherwise — olai advertised nothing\n- agent.ts auto-answered every request_permission with the first allow option, which would have silently approved ExitPlanMode into \"auto\" mode\n- Out of scope: elicitation.url, permission settings UI\n- Pairs with orchestrator-in-chat\n","see":["chat","orchestrator-in-chat"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-commit-manual","parent":"feat-git","ord":"a3","title":"The MCP face never got manual commits","done":"2026-08-12T09:34:34-04:00","desc":"**Shipped in PR #116** (squash 324f8b5, merged 2026-08-12T13:33:55Z, human-approved).\n- Discovered mid-work that #83 had been reverted entirely (see the RCA); after #114 restored it, this PR delivered the original scope\n- olai mcp takes the same `--commit=off|manual|auto` tri-state as olai web, manual default, `--no-commit` still meaning off\n- The commit verb joins the MCP tool table (last in TOOLS, after #117's mirror ops) calling the one Ops.commit — message required\n  - Reply reports the swept pending summary\n  - Refuses with reason on a busy repository\n- pending/last/writer-intent readable identically over MCP per the HACKING consistency rule\n- Applied.why under manual mode reads as expected-pending, never as a git error\n- **Byte-identical-faces test:** both faces produce identical commits for the same pending set\n- **CI caught a real startup race:** first pending read accepted the unpublished seed and asserted Off against Ready (darwin-only timing) — fixed by waiting for a published value, README teaches the pattern\n- **Final leg:** merged past #109/#112/#115/#117/#118/#119\n  - Roadmap verified byte-identical to master by blob hash\n  - Noted that origin/master advancing by push mid-merge (shared refs across worktrees) can shortchange a merge — the byte-hash check catches it\n- **NEXT:** reconnect the olai MCP server to activate manual mode — one commit per orchestration beat via the commit verb — and #117's mirror ops\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-drop-files","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"a4","title":"Drag and drop files into the chat","done":"2026-08-12T17:42:12-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as PR #126**, squash 4851ad5 (2026-08-12). Drop lands on the existing attachment machinery — nothing new below the gesture.\n- The panel body (header excluded) is the drop target with a visible affordance\n- enter/leave COUNTED (not flagged — crossing transcript rows is one drag; sabotaging the counter to a boolean fails the e2e)\n- dragend clears a cancelled drag's overlay (both endings asserted)\n- Text drags left alone\n- Multi-file drops attach in order all the way to the order the agent reads them\n- **Refusals survive each other:** the batch sorts through the ONE shared gate, Chat.attach answers (stored/refused/gone) instead of drawing, and holding.take says every refusal once on the panel's one line\n  - Closes a real silent-loss path (file 3 used to rub out file 2's reason; the reviewer proved nothing went red without its test, so the fix is pinned by a take unit test with type+size reasons)\n- **MID-FLIGHT HUMAN RULING** (the human hit it driving the build): the gate widened beyond pictures\n  - attachmentRejection now takes DOCUMENT_EXTENSIONS (.pdf .txt .md .csv .json) with honest name+size chips\n  - The picker's accept= matches the gate\n  - .svg keeps its scriptable-document refusal\n  - The 50 MB cap stays\n  - Loosening the gate to accept .svg turns four tests red\n- **Two reviewer rounds:** initial — one MUST-FIX + the dragend bug upgraded by the orchestrator; re-verify 1 and 2 both \"the PR stands clean\", every fix sabotage-verified\n- CI green both platforms at each head\n- Human approved 2026-08-12\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"adapter-interpret","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"a5","title":"Adapter interpretation out of agent.ts: one testable module #techdebt","done":"2026-08-12T15:25:48-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as PR #125**, squash e7fc004 (2026-08-12) — same day the kitchen-sinks debate ratified it (debates/kitchen-sinks/conclusion.md item 4; filed and dispatched on the human's word).\n- packages/chat/src/interpret.ts now owns the adapter's interpretation as pure functions:\n  - `allowedWithoutAsking` (the debate's shouldBypass, renamed because it answers with WHICH option, never a boolean — positive recognition of `mcp__<server>__` against the given names, never the first allow-flavoured option, so plan mode's \"Ready to code?\" cannot silently flip the session to auto)\n  - `toolNameIn` (`_meta.claudeCode.toolName`)\n  - `liveModelIn`/`modelPickerIn`/`labelsOf` (the forwarded CLI init on `_claude/sdkMessage` + the free-form \"model\" config select)\n  - Plus `NEW_SESSION_META`/`SDK_MESSAGE`/`BYPASS_MODE`\n  - Two strays (`id===\"model\"`, `bypassPermissions`) the author proved are adapter vocabulary, not protocol (SessionConfigId and SessionModeId are free-form strings; bypassPermissions appears nowhere in the SDK)\n- 22 unit tests, no subprocess — the safety rule is unit-testable for the first time\n- `onPermission` is four lines\n- agent.ts 1119→1033 with all closure state (session lifecycle, toolNames map, model debounce) unmoved\n- interpret.ts deliberately NOT on the package's export socket\n- **The reviewer passed it with zero MUST-FIX** after two sabotage probes (dropping the ours gate and weakening the prefix match both went red) and arm-by-arm equivalence against the old inline logic\n- Zero behavior change; e2e green throughout\n- Human pre-approved on the green gate\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-edit-diffs","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"a6","title":"Chat shows the agent's file-edit diffs, trimmed, expand on click","done":"2026-08-12T22:05:05-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #130 (c7f8fdb), squash-merged 2026-08-13. Two previews, two vocabularies, one fold idiom — as ratified.\n\n- **Direct file edits**: ACP's diff block travels STRUCTURED (FileDiff: path + oldText/newText); the panel renders Claude-Code-style — trimmed to 6 rows, unchanged runs collapsed into gaps first, expanded in place on click. The line diff is a hand-rolled prefix/suffix-strip + suffix-table LCS (~100-line walk; the diff micro-deps bring character algorithms and patch application for one function — same trade as @olai/git over simple-git). Bounded: over budget says \"rewritten whole\" rather than a wrong diff.\n- **Olai MCP writes**: never a text diff — the node-level story (marked done / note rewritten / moved) via Applied.sort on the ops reply, derived by the same changesOf that classifies commit-panel rows; SAID/GLYPH moved to changes.ts, ONE table for both panels. The never-rule is true of the FILE, not just the ops path: a direct Edit on a .jsonl routes to the story row (fileKind → OutlineDiff).\n- **Review**: 1 MUST-FIX (no reconstruction property — a diagonal-index sabotage left all ten tests green; the reviewer property-checked the implementation itself over 22 cases first) + 6 NICE-TO-HAVEs, ALL taken including two upgraded (the .jsonl file-rule; docs/chat.md's now-false \"no filesystem\" paragraph). DELTA-OK. /simplify caught a literal NUL byte that made folds.ts git-binary.\n- **Conflict round**: #129 moved master; resolved keeping both docs truths (+2/−2), full suite on the merged head, CI 10/10 at 6d8fafd.\n- **Evidence** (verified by the orchestrator): trimmed card, in-place expansion, set_done story row with the outline agreeing beside it, and the .jsonl fallback — archived to the session scratchpad.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"ask-vocabulary","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"a7","title":"@olai/acp: the ask vocabulary moves to the wall that speaks ACP","done":"2026-08-13T15:25:45-04:00","desc":"Debate-ratified 2026-08-13 (item 2); Position A resolved by the human to fable's wall. **Shipped as PR #144 (squash fbbc15a), 2026-08-13.**\n- New workspace package `@olai/acp` owns the protocol's words:\n  - AskField/AskChoice/AskAnswer/AskOutcome/YES_NO on `./wire` (surface re-exports — no consumer moved an import).\n  - FileDiff judged same-tenant with the argument written at the declaration.\n  - asks/diffs projections + Form/Refused on the main entry.\n- **UsageFailure** translated at the seam, not moved: `Refused` (a plain value, never on a wire or Effect channel) is minted into UsageFailure in exactly one place (`questions.ts`) and read in one (`agent.ts`).\n- **The boundary is machine-checked:** a six-claim manifest test over one tree scan (position-based specifiers + `Bun.Transpiler.scanImports`).\n  - No `@olai/*` import may appear inside acp.\n  - SDK runtime imports only in the subprocess files; matcher covers SDK subpaths.\n- **Pipeline:**\n  - Grok review — zero MUST-FIX; the boundary judgment verified file-by-file against Position A (and the losing floor position used to sharpen the cut).\n  - All four NTHs taken red-first (subpath matcher via the reviewer's own sabotage). DELTA-OK twice.\n  - Parity: 1224 unit, 384 e2e twice (local + CI), packaged-binary smoke; CI green at 8afbc08 on kolu-ci-1.\n  - One test-lane flake (pre-existing kolu fixture's SDK parse noise) judged unrelated and green on rerun.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-subjects","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"a8","title":"One way to say \"this is about that\": chats, nodes, notes #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- One association mechanism across three pairs: chat↔node (resume a node's chat from its ••• menu), node↔note (likely an edge like see/after), chat↔note (reduces to the other two).\n- Brainstorm: docs/brainstorming/associations.md. Awaits ratification.","changed":"2026-08-21T17:05:58-04:00"}
{"id":"reads-on-the-floor","parent":"surface-mcp","ord":"a1","title":"Query-shaped reads move to the format floor","done":"2026-08-14T22:41:42-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #167 (2026-08-14), recorded with THREE traps:\n1. The shared read-request vocabulary must go to `@olai/format`, NOT `@olai/ops`.\n2. `Applied` cannot be included — the two sides are deliberately different types.\n3. An Outline schema in `format/searching.ts` would collide with the Outline the package already exports from `set.ts:62` via `index.ts`.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #170, squashed at head 95d69fc — a pure refactor by the end.\n  - All three traps respected.\n  - **Drift property** proven by experiment and extended twice by the review round.\n    - The `as SearchHit` cast became an annotation (a SearchHit-only field now fails ops+web+server where it compiled clean before).\n    - `NodeContext` borrows Found's field schemas (dropping `Found.path` now fails `@olai/chat` too).\n- **Review:** Grok + opencode, zero blocking, every nit fixed or answered on the record; all commits verified standalone.\n- CI 9/9 required green at 95d69fc.\n- **One behavior change the branch had carried** — trimming `list_outlines`' torn-file answer — was REVERTED before merge (nothing unratified lands overnight) and became its own #human node.\n- **The three concurred declines** became their own #techdebt nodes: the four-way `{file,line}` spelling, `read()`'s request-half inference, `outlines()`'s O(files × nodes) walk.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"per-face-expose","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"a7","title":"Upstream: serveSurfaceApp cannot scope a verb per face #upstream #human","done":"2026-08-15T09:03:32-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #167 (2026-08-14): the 18 write tools have no surface procedure, and giving them one puts the ops request vocabulary on the surface.\n- `serveSurfaceApp` took handlers whole with no expose list, so every open tab could call every verb.\n- **DONE 2026-08-15:** the human approved and kolu PR [#2170](https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2170) is squash-merged at bfb4eb56.\n  - `@kolu/surface/expose` gives every serving face the same ExposeMap grammar (`classifyExpose`), a checked `FaceExposure` at the handler seam, `SurfaceMemberNotExposed` as the per-request refusal.\n  - The night's review round contributed one real fix (`Object.prototype` keys no longer listable as members).\n  - Drishti pair srid/drishti#142 re-pinned to bfb4eb56 (tarball byte-identical to the reviewed tree) and MERGED on the human's word; lane torn down clean.\n- Issue [#2169](https://github.com/juspay/kolu/issues/2169) STAYS OPEN for the writable-primitive-on-gated-face spelling.\n  - The PR's `Closes #2169` auto-closed it at merge and the author reopened it with the landed-vs-open split written out.\n- **LESSON**, worth a HACKING line someday: a multi-slice issue wants \"Part of #n\" in PR bodies, never \"Closes #n\".\n- Two framework-shape questions stay recorded on #2170 for srid (one expose currency across faces; expose-required + exposeEverything), cheapest while a drishti gate is open.\n- **What this unblocked:** mcp-bridge, dispatched the same day.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-bridge","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"a8","title":"The bridge shape: an external agent attaches to the RUNNING olai","done":"2026-08-15T11:16:32-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #167 (2026-08-14). UNBLOCKED 2026-08-15 by kolu #2170 (bfb4eb56); ratified as ONE PR, three stages.\n- **Now** (2026-08-15):\n  - Kolu terminal: `cd13fd33` (Claude Opus, YOLO), olai repo, branch `mcp-bridge`.\n  - PR: #175 — pin bump.\n    - ALL write verbs (19, not the node's 18 — md-editing postdates it, noted in code) as surface procedures.\n    - MCP face exposed, browser face denied.\n    - The bridge: `olai mcp` attaches to a running server over the unix socket, boots its own store only when none runs.\n    - Design doc: `docs/brainstorming/mcp-bridge.md`.\n  - **Audit correction** carried honestly: the 418 MB two-store price was misread.\n    - An `olai mcp` over an EMPTY directory is already 213.8 MiB (Bun runtime, not corpus); memory does not halve.\n    - The fd story stays with bun-watcher-bump (the bridge's remaining 1048 descriptors are the watcher's).\n  - **Decisions for srid at fielding:**\n    - Writer became a per-FACE binding (`ops.commit` twin deleted — it existed only to carry the field and had drifted on its error channel).\n    - The three READS became procedures too (stage 3 could not leave them behind).\n  - **Deferred on the record:**\n    - `socket.ts:86` realpath vs `directory.ts:16` string-trim — two canonicalisations of \"which directory\" (symlink → same socket, different chat memory), pre-existing, not widened.\n    - chat-agent face's writer has no e2e trailer test (fenced only, same as before).\n    - Socket latency unmeasured, said so in the doc.\n  - **Stage:** #review — Grok (`dc5279c5`) and opencode (`0be27fed`), briefed to run the DRY drift experiment themselves, re-verify the 213.8 MiB baseline, and attack the canonicalisation seam.\n  - **CI:** 8/9 at 47c5d52c with e2e finishing under the author's monitor (10/10 at both preceding heads).\n  - **Then:** FIELDED to the human — the orchestrator merges only on his word.","after":["per-face-expose"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"watcher-fd-cost","parent":"surface-mcp","ord":"a4","title":"The recursive watcher holds one fd per served file, per store, for life #techdebt","done":"2026-08-14T23:32:02-04:00","desc":"FINDING from PR #167's two-store measurement (2026-08-14): the store's recursive watcher holds one open fd per served file, per store, for the process's lifetime.\n- 14 fds with `watch:false` vs 1050 with `watch:true` on a 1020-file vault.\n- **CLOSED 2026-08-14** (night slate) as an investigation, per the human's small-or-stop ruling — NO CODE, one doc: PR #173, squashed at df2a646, `docs/brainstorming/watcher-fd-cost.md`.\n- **The cost is BUN'S:** 1.3.13's `fs.watch` routes through Bun's internal bundler watcher, one `open(2)` per path under the ROOT (.git and node_modules included — the real multiplier).\n  - Bun 1.3.14's rewrite onto inotify/FSEvents/kqueue drops it to ~15 descriptors and closes the post-boot-subdir blind spot.\n- Per-directory watching, the brief's own proposal, measured at identical cost on 1.3.13 — no small fix existed.\n- **Both reviewers reproduced every conclusion independently** (fact-check round: nits only, all re-measured and folded, one honest 13-fd run-divergence explained in the doc).\n  - Grok's intelligence about nixpkgs#519796 being held on a bun-compile SIGSEGV olai wouldn't hit is left in the review record.\n- **Successor nodes:** bun-watcher-bump (#human, the ruling) and watcher-postboot-blind (the bug the bump also fixes).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"torn-file-answer-trim","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"a9","title":"list_outlines answers an unreadable file with meaningless zeros #human #next #grok","done":"2026-08-22T16:43:30-04:00","desc":"- An unreadable outline answers `{file, nodes: 0, roots: [], unreadable}` — the zeros are noise beside the flag.\n- A fix to `{file, unreadable}` was written and verified safe (both consumers read `.file` only), then reverted pending the human's word.\n- Either shape is one small commit; the case is preserved in reading.ts, format/README.md:270 and commit 525f737a.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as 3b9fe9ab (ruled {file, unreadable}; list_documents' torn row matches)","changed":"2026-08-22T16:43:30-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/350"}}
{"id":"chat-token-usage","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"a9","title":"Chat shows token usage, so /compact stops being a guess","done":"2026-08-15T12:31:51-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 by the human: the chat gave no view of context consumption, so /compact was a guess.\n\n- **MERGED** 2026-08-15 (pre-approved by the human): PR #178, squashed at fcbb155f.\n- Header draws the newest usage_update frame as a FRACTION (22k/1M) beside the model.\n  - A percentage was rejected on captured evidence: the adapter corrects the window mid-conversation (1000000 → 200000 on the wire), and a percentage read 2% on both sides of a fivefold drop in real headroom.\n- Read in @olai/acp (any agent may send usage); newest frame wins — pinned MID-TURN with a hold verb after Grok caught the fake agent reproducing only half the correction, sabotage-verified both directions.\n- cost arrives on the wire and is deliberately undrawn, with a unit test asserting the drop.\n- **Reviews:** Grok (2 findings + the deeper recursion of its own fix) and opencode (1 blocking) — all addressed with per-finding replies.\n  - The round also produced the pending-review-draft lesson (a review created without a submit event sits invisible — the orchestrator submitted it by API) and the detached-HEAD reviewer hazard.\n- **Deferred** in the PR body:\n  - No compaction-threshold cue yet (wants the human's eye on a real session).\n  - A loaded conversation shows nothing until its first turn (session/load replays without a usage frame — documented where a person meets it).","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"olai-subscribes","parent":"feat-orch","ord":"aC","title":"PR: olai watches kolu's terminals itself and updates lane marks","todo":true,"desc":"- The olai server subscribes to kolu's terminal/urgency feeds and updates lane step nodes live — no agent babysitting terminals.\n- Retires the detached watcher shells and hand-flipped marks.\n- Needs mcp-bridge's plumbing first.","after":["lane-cloning","mcp-bridge"],"changed":"2026-08-26T10:43:02-04:00","custom":{"blocker-gone":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: \"needs mcp-bridge's plumbing first\" — mcp-bridge is done (2026-08-15), the blocker is gone; what this PR retires today is the kolu watch background Monitor + the supervision-watcher ledger (instructions.md's ONLY-wake-mechanism), per orchestrator.md rev 2's olai-subscribes-to-padi design"}}
{"id":"chat-at-completion","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aA","title":"Chat: typing @ completes file paths into the message","done":"2026-08-17T00:31:16-04:00","desc":"Requested 2026-08-16.\n- In the chat input, typing `@` should open a completion of the served directory's files (the same set the sidebar knows: outlines and documents), filtered as you type, inserting the path into the message — the way Claude Code's own `@` works in the terminal.\n- **Precedent:** the chat client already has a completion pattern to lean on — the editor's tag autocomplete (input-widgets).\n- **No new server surface needed:** the file list is already on the wire for free — the `outlines` collection's keys plus the `documents` collection's key set.\n- **Decide alongside:** whether a completed `@path` is plain text the agent reads, or carries the same attach semantics the `+` button has.","created":"2026-08-16T11:19:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/213"}}
{"id":"chat-rewind","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aB","title":"Chat: no /rewind yet — waiting on the adapter","todo":true,"desc":"- The chat has no rewind verb; the pinned adapter hasn't shipped one either (its id-mapping plumbing exists but is unused). The CLI's /rewind is terminal-only.\n- Two paths: wait for the adapter's verb (check on each pin bump), or offer \"branch this conversation\" today via `unstable_forkSession`.\n- The human hasn't asked for the branch button; it becomes a lane on their word.","created":"2026-08-16T14:03:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:08:20-04:00","custom":{"pin-gap":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the gap is real (no rewind/forkSession under packages/) but the check-on-bump premise is stale — the pin sits at 0.66.0 while npm latest is 0.70.0, and the pin now carries a local patch (acp/patches/, #365): a bump check is OWED and must re-apply the patch"}}
{"id":"self-edit","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"a0","title":"Keyboard editing","done":"2026-08-12T09:15:56-04:00","desc":"Shipped in PR #109 (squash a1d18f7, merged 2026-08-12T13:13:53Z, human-approved).\n- **The Workflowy editing loop through the ops layer:** Enter (new sibling as draft — never writes a blank record), Tab/Shift+Tab indent/outdent, Alt+Shift+↑↓ move, Ctrl+Enter toggle done, ↑↓ row walking with visible caret, Escape\n- titles edit inline via input overlay, descs edit inline on click (post-review fix)\n- drafts commit on blur/Enter/idle and survive a REFUSED write\n- every structural key is one op through the write gate — no optimistic echo\n- **edit.apply intent seam:** client sends indent/outdent/move intents, server resolves placement against the judged snapshot (mirror-anchor bugs fixed under adversarial review)\n- One keyboard registry joined with #104's map; ⌘K/⌘\\/⌘J pinned by test\n- 18 new e2e + unit coverage; 858 unit / 252 e2e green on the merged tree\n- **Human's post-test fixes folded in:** sibling indent, Shift+Enter inline (no box), desc click-to-edit, visible caret\n- DELETE ABSENT by ruling; split/merge/undo/multi-select/drag-drop deferred\n- **Final leg note:** git rerere silently auto-resolved the roadmap during the master merge — caught and restored byte-for-byte; wariness recorded for future merges","after":["chat"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"split-merge","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"a1","title":"Split & merge","done":"2026-08-14T00:46:59-04:00","desc":"Enter mid-text splits a node in two; Backspace at line start merges into the previous sibling.\n- Compound ops (split_node/merge_node) over the ops layer, both faces calling the same op (deferred 2026-08-09 out of keyboard-editing)\n\n**MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, SIMPLE — autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #157, squashed.\n- **Grok review:** 2 blocking (split-at-a-mirror wrote in the target's home file and lost the caret — now follows the 'Enter on a mirror makes a sibling of the PLACEMENT' rule; Backspace on an uncommitted typed row was swallowed — merge now commits the draft first), 4 nits, all addressed at 43c1bae with fail-then-pass proof\n- **Undo design settled by the reviewer:** split's inverse stays merge-as-inverse (remove + was-guarded title would break redo placement); the residual was-hole is documented in inverseOf's split arm — THE HUMAN MAY OVERRULE\n- Nine scope decisions documented on the PR (merge targets previous sibling, not Workflowy's previous visible row; Enter-at-head stays add; etc.)\n- CI 9/9 required green; 1362 unit tests, 437 e2e scenarios; evidence page on the PR","after":["self-edit"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"undo","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"a2","title":"Undo","done":"2026-08-12T13:23:05-04:00","desc":"Shipped in PR #120 (squash b77f929, merged 2026-08-12T17:22:33Z, human-approved with the un-create framing ratified by that approval).\n- **Undo/redo as an intent-inverse stack:** every web edit — structural AND, after the human's live finding, committed title/desc text — records its server-derived inverse at apply time; ⌘Z replays the inverse through the same edit.apply gate against the current snapshot, ⌘⇧Z symmetric; refusals verbatim over the page\n- **Four review rounds (Grok), each closing a real defect with a regression test proven red:**\n  1. redo pollution — a structural op landing mid-replay repopulated the cleared redo side; fixed by putting ALL stack mutations through one serial queue, making the window unobservable\n  2. ledger purity\n  3. the human's finding — 'drafts excluded' had over-excluded committed text ops; title/desc inverses added with a was guard (undo of a retyped row refuses naming the current text)\n  4. the was guard's TOCTOU across ops.run StaleWrite retries — re-checked on every plan attempt\n- **Un-create:** ⌘Z on a row this session created archives it (childless only, GONE aside, cannot be redone — unarchive is parity-unarchive); NO delete key, deferral stays open and docs say so (docs/editing.md, new under #123's split)\n- **Judgment calls ratified in review:** undo of done re-derives the stamp (no op writes a chosen mark value — consistency); position restored as placement (parent + after neighbour), not byte-identical ord\n- Stack: session-local, depth 100, cleared on outline switch, dead in drafts/forms/palette\n- 920 unit + 279 e2e at merge; CI green both platforms at the SHIP head","after":["self-edit"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"dragdrop-multiselect","parent":"feat-mouse","ord":"a1","title":"Drag-drop & multi-select","done":"2026-08-14T09:44:30-04:00","desc":"Drag a node to move it with its subtree; Workflowy's multi-select gestures with bulk complete/move/indent/put-away.\n\n**MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #159, the human approved, squashed at bbfeec70 after resolving against master's #161/#163/#164):\n- a drop is a gap plus a depth; carried rows leave the candidate set where rows are measured (cross-file rows too — a mirror is not a parent, and reordering inside a mirror lands in its home file)\n- pick-XOR-caret enforced in open/start; the Trash confirm keys on the pick's identity\n- Grok review was 3 blocking + 3 nits, all addressed with fail-then-pass proof\n- **In the master merge** it adopted #164's canonical readers/steps (its own copies deleted), took LAYER.row/LAYER.chrome for its lines, and recorded why the refusal bar does not ride saying.ts (a run-stopper follows UndoSaid's no-fade rule) while gaining the missing aria-live\n- Its own flake caveat was closed by #164: 478/478 under the load that used to drop scenarios\n- CI 9/9 required green at bbfeec70\n- **Deferred** (named on the PR, still open): drag-across marquee, touch drag, edge auto-scroll, a delete key (the human's ruling wanted), tone/role unification across five said surfaces","after":["self-edit"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"input-widgets","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"a3","title":"Input affordances","done":"2026-08-14T10:04:48-04:00","desc":"The Workflowy input widgets: `!` natural-language date list (set_date), `#`/`@` tag autocomplete, `((` mirror-creation search (add_mirror — parity nobody had filed: the surface could retire a placement it had no way to make).\n\n**MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #160, the human approved, squashed at 5af9f68 after resolving against master's #159/#161/#163/#164):\n- built over the ops layer; the palette's list-cursor machinery grew a third keys.ts layer and absorbed two unmigrated copies\n- a latent blur-swallow bug fixed with a timing-free redraws.test.ts (proved fail-then-pass)\n- feb 29 walks to the next leap year\n- **In the master merge** it adopted #164's readers/steps and taught `answering` the completion-list receipt (theListIsGone — one spelling of \"no list\" for three callers), took LAYER.row for the completion popup (with the argued reason the error line does NOT ride saying.ts — it mirrors a live failure, not a lingering said), and closed two parity entries in the brainstorming inventory\n- Grok review was 1 blocking + 5 nits, all addressed\n- CI 9/9 required green at 5af9f68; 497 e2e scenarios, 1491 unit tests on the merged tree\n- **Deferred** (named on the PR): `!` opens the list only, not the calendar; parity-see/parity-after want this widget family but neither verb is on the wire; unmirror's inverse still empty (reason in the arm)","after":["self-edit"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"palette","parent":"feat-mouse","ord":"a4","title":"Command palette #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-14T10:24:50-04:00","desc":"Ctrl+K palette over ops and navigation.\n- **History:** panels shipped the ⌘K shell; jump-to-node type-ahead shipped with it (fact-checked 2026-08-13); this item delivered the remaining command-ACTIONS half\n\n**MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #162, the human approved, squashed at 5b99551 after resolving against master's #159/#160/#161/#163/#164):\n- the ••• menu's verbs as palette commands on the zoomed context (palette/ops.ts)\n- quick capture with racket `olai add`-to-Inbox parity; the Inbox convention written in docs/format.md and on the MCP tool text\n- Grok review was 1 blocking (capture in-flight guard) + 3 nits, all addressed with fail-then-pass proof\n- The master merge kept both palette features intact (23/23 palette scenarios) on #160's third keys layer, with the argued exception recorded for the one write whose promise is that the reader doesn't move\n- CI 9/9 required green at 5b99551; 520 e2e scenarios, 1263 unit tests on the merged tree\n- Evidence artifact: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/524e3160-f738-4b64-b0e6-eb5300eb3bdf (behaviour current; its shot counts predate the final master merge)\n- **Deferred**, named on the PR: op rows are the zoomed node's only; the residual confirm-shell duplication is a `<p>` and a flex row","after":["navigation","panels"],"see":["search","panels"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"md-editing","parent":"feat-docs","ord":"aB","title":"Documents become writable: create and edit .md from olai","done":"2026-08-13T19:26:25-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-12 on the human's word. **Shipped as PR #148 (squash 10fd1fbf), 2026-08-13.**\n- Documents are writable end to end through the one ops path on both faces: `write_document`/`create_document` on MCP and the web editor drive the same planner → store.commit → audit trail (X-Olai-Writer)\n- The was-guard refuses an external edit (vim mid-session) in words with an explicit \"Overwrite what is there\" (which clobbers the CURRENT disk, verified)\n- A bare calendar day mints that day's note per the vault's own convention (path inferred from the newest daily note)\n- Dirty .md files ride the existing commit flow\n- **The review's MUST-FIX:** document→document navigation reused the Solid page instance (mint hand-off broken, cross-file draft possible)\n  - Fixed by construction (keyed identity) with three scenarios, measured against pre-fix code (the cross-file draft was the deterministic red; the creation doors had been green by frame-ordering luck)\n- Seven+ sabotage-verified pins; CI green at merge head e14e0800 on kolu-ci-1; 1249 unit, 396 e2e\n- **Recorded, not fixed (pre-existing):** fs.watch only sees a brand-new subdirectory on the next probe — the store's 60s backstop covers it\n- Follow-up filed: md-rich-editing\n","see":["daily-notes","commit-whole-repo"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"menu-verbs","parent":"feat-mouse","ord":"a3","title":"The ••• menu learns to write: marks, clear-date, remove-placement, archive, copy-as-text","done":"2026-08-12T14:24:01-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as PR #124**, squash 60631fe (2026-08-12). The mouse's first write path: the ••• menu gained five verbs.\n- Contextual mark section (todo/doing/complete/clear, current mark hidden, ops refusals verbatim in the said line)\n- Clear-date (dated rows only)\n- Remove-placement (mirror rows only, op's own fence)\n- Archive (subtree, inline confirm naming DERIVED descendant count — the author's own /simplify pass caught the count reading rendered rows under done-hidden — honest restore sentence since unarchive does not exist)\n- Copy-as-text (tab-indented plain text, target's subtree on a mirror)\n- **Closed four editor-op-parity children for the mouse:** parity-archive, parity-date (removal half), parity-marks (menu half), parity-remove-mirror\n- The menu moved to web/src/client/menu/ (NodeMenu + verbs/actions/writes/subtree, unit-tested)\n- **Reconciled with #120 at merge:**\n  - Mark collapsed to ONE arm and one resolver spoken by both callers\n  - Archive vs remove stay two verbs with different fences\n  - inverseOf extended so a cleared date is restored as the date it cleared\n  - Menu writes record onto the same ⌘Z stack\n- Survived a 10-point adversarial review and two master syncs (#120's 40-file, #122's 49-file)\n- **CI saga:** two red x86_64-linux e2e legs turned out to be the author's own harness error (odu client wrapped in timeout 600, killing the lane mid-suite)\n  - Proven by a controlled experiment on the CI host itself: master control 7/7 clean, branch equally clean once the timeout wrapper was removed\n  - Final gate 21/21 contexts green both platforms\n- Human approved 2026-08-12\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"multiselect-completion","parent":"feat-mouse","ord":"a2","title":"Picking completed: drag-across marquee, edge auto-scroll, touch drag","done":"2026-08-14T16:33:15-04:00","desc":"The deferrals PR #159 named, taken up 2026-08-14 at the human's word. **MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #169, the human approved, squashed at e9adceb).\n- **Drag-across marquee**: allowlist not preventDefault; band not box; the flat page gains its rail at the ul so depth 0 sweeps like everywhere else.\n- **Edge auto-scroll**: window decides whether, page decides where; still pointer keeps scrolling.\n- **Touch drag**: long-press on the bullet lifts the row; scroll claimed at the deadline with non-passive touchmove, not `touch-action:none`; the mutation-proven fence green with a sister scenario.\n- **Design ruling shipped panel-converged:** the bullet is the one drag handle on all devices (both reviewers independently recommended it).\n- Panel grok 0+2 / opencode 0+3, union addressed; the `userSelect` single-writer premise is a `claims.test.ts` sweep.\n- CI 9/9 at e9adceb; 551 scenarios / 4110 steps.\n- **Still deferred:** the delete key (the human's ruling), tone/role unification, sweep-union modifier, finger-sweep (permanent no).","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"move-to-picker","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"a4","title":"Move-to picker: fuzzy-search a new parent anywhere, from the keyboard","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:19-04:00","desc":"Approved overnight 2026-08-17.\n\n- **Feature:** a keyboard dialog (Workflowy's ctrl-shift-M) — invoke on the current node, fuzzy-search every node across all outlines as a destination, Enter moves the node (with its subtree) under the chosen parent.\n- **Reuse:** the search machinery; the move is the existing move op.\n- **Cross-file moves:** refuse with a clear message if the op layer cannot express them (outlines are independent trees — archiving is what crosses files).\n- Say so in the dialog rather than hiding the limit.","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00","custom":{"merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/7d6706c1a","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/245"}}
{"id":"duplicate-subtree","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"a5","title":"Duplicate subtree: copy a node and everything under it in one action","done":"2026-08-18T10:06:54-04:00","desc":"Approved overnight 2026-08-17. One keyboard/menu action clones the current node and its whole subtree as a sibling below (fresh ids throughout, marks preserved or reset? — the author decides and documents; Workflowy preserves). Mirrors under the copied subtree: copy the placement, not the identity. For templates and repeated structures.","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"recurring-dates","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"a6","title":"Recurring dates: a repeat rule on dated nodes — done spawns the next occurrence","done":"2026-08-18T10:06:54-04:00","desc":"Approved overnight 2026-08-17.\n\n- **Feature:** a dated node gains an optional repeat rule (every day / week on Mon / month / year) — keep the grammar small and spelled in the file.\n- **Completing it:** stamps done AND creates the next occurrence at the next date (a fresh node, so the journal keeps the honest history of each completion).\n- Agenda and daily pages show the next occurrence like any dated node.\n- Web editing of the rule beside the date; MCP parity in the same PR.","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"md-second-class","parent":"feat-docs","ord":"aD","title":"Where markdown still trails outlines #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- Audit (2026-08-18, re-verified 08-19 — the full capability table lives in this node's git history): markdown is first-class where a file is treated as a file, second-class where content is reasoned about.\n- Much has shipped since filing: document addresses, search over bodies, palette rows, backlinks (#251, #253, #256, #258).\n- Still open, each needing its own ruling before PR-shaped children split off:\n  - The `node.doc` field: nobody can write it, no read tool reports it, and node.ts:199 documents a capture door that doesn't exist.\n  - Documents as see/after edge targets.\n  - Structure verbs for a .md: move, rename, trash.\n  - Chat: doc paths in prose and tool frames aren't pressable; documents aren't armable.\n  - The README never says markdown.\n- Design arc: brainstorming/first-class-documents.md (ruled with the human 2026-08-19).","see":["search-document-bodies"],"created":"2026-08-18T18:51:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:08:22-04:00","custom":{"brainstorm":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md — the hierarchy (Document ⊃ OutlineDocument/MarkdownDocument), the [document]#[element] address grammar, derived md face now, frontmatter later (ruled with the human 2026-08-19)","citation-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: the \"node.ts:199 documents a capture door that doesn't exist\" bullet is stale — the doc door now sits at node.ts:217 reading \"a node names its document when it is captured; write_document writes what is in it\"; the rest of the open list still verifies (no op writes node.doc; no document move/rename/trash in tools.ts)"}}
{"id":"parity-read-documents","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a0","title":"MCP reads documents: list_documents + read_document","done":"2026-08-19T11:01:25-04:00","desc":"Closes the table's \"2 of 30 tools, no read, no list\" row's read half.\n\n- An agent can now list the documents the directory serves and read one whole.\n- A missing path refuses in the tools' own voice.\n- `face.ts`'s charter says the honest thing (\"nodes and whole documents, never bytes\") with a test pinning the retired \"no file access\" sentence.\n- **Flag argued in surface/ops.ts:** `read_document` and the documents collection resource answer differently on purpose (request-shaped vs render-shaped).","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"overnight-3 (parity pick a)","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/191d7677","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/251"}}
{"id":"parity-palette-documents","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a1","title":"A document is a row in the ⌘K box, matched by its name","done":"2026-08-19T11:01:28-04:00","desc":"Closes the table's \"zero document rows in the palette\" row.\n\n- The palette and the header search box share one module: a served `.md`/`.html` matches by title/filename and opens its page.\n- The served-path matcher moved to `file/matching.ts` beside the `@` completion.\n- **The create row went NO** — the palette has no create row for outlines either, so offering one to documents alone would invert the imbalance, not remove it (argued on the PR and in docs/search.md).\n- **Doctrine held:** the node grammar reads no `.md` body.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"overnight-3 (parity pick b)","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/4a9ae71b","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/253"}}
{"id":"fcd-pr1-addresses","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a2","title":"Addresses: the [document]#[element] grammar, URL = / + address — PR 1 of first-class documents","done":"2026-08-19T14:38:19-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-19 on the human's word, to Opus.\n\n- **Scope:** the brainstorm's \"PR 1 — addresses\", self-contained.\n  - The branded primitives and the Address sum with `parseAddress`/`printAddress` and the bijection test.\n  - `routes.ts` rebuilt so a content URL is `/` + address.\n  - `/o/` `/doc/` `/n/` deleted in the same diff.\n  - `Pins.olai` titles swept to the new spelling.\n- Compat break blessed by the human.\n\n**pr** — (approved by the human 2026-08-19; 874/874 e2e, evidence visually verified)","created":"2026-08-19T12:43:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","branch":"fcd-addresses","from":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/675886e0","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/256","terminal":"6079d86f-0a99-44ae-b591-5c2d7f0a4a25"}}
{"id":"fcd-pr2-face","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a3","title":"The face: Document = Outline | Markdown, the set serves one collection — PR 2 of first-class documents","done":"2026-08-19T17:09:45-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-19 on the human's word, to Opus, immediately after PR 1 (#256) merged.\n\n- **Scope:** the brainstorm's \"PR 2 — the face\", self-contained.\n  - The `Outline | Markdown` sum with the derived markdown face.\n  - The set serves it as THE collection, with the parallel nodes/documents exports deleted and every importer migrated.\n  - Search walks Document and hits carry addresses (closes search-document-bodies).\n  - Palette and backlinks ride the same index.\n- **Carries PR 1's two named deferrals that belong here:**\n  - Route's three content arms collapse toward one Address-carrying arm.\n  - `DocumentPath`'s constructor rule moves into a schema filter the day an Address is decoded off a wire.\n\n**pr** — (approved by the human 2026-08-19; grok + opencode both do-not-object; evidence visually verified; final head df2b94a6 was the conflict-free master merge with #257)","created":"2026-08-19T14:38:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","branch":"fcd-face","from":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/29f4ec38","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/258"}}
{"id":"md-yaml-frontmatter","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a4","title":"YAML frontmatter: parsed nowhere, skipped by exactly one scanner — the ruled-later half of first-class documents","done":"2026-08-20T19:53:31-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 from a full-repo markdown survey on the human's ask. Frontmatter is not parsed, not rendered, not stripped — only *skipped*, in one place.\n\n**What exists today:**\n- The only frontmatter-aware code is `format/src/slug.ts:166-186` — `headingsIn` skips a leading `---` block so `title: x` above the closing `---` is not misread as a setext heading. Its own comment: \"Nothing here READS frontmatter.\"\n- No `remark-frontmatter`, `gray-matter`, `js-yaml` or `yaml` dependency in any package.json.\n- Dead leftover: `FRONTMATTER_OPENS = 4` at `slug.ts:258` is declared and referenced nowhere.\n- The hole is stated as deliberate in `format/src/document.ts:82-86`, `docs/format.md:216`, `docs/search.md:113`, `docs/brainstorming/first-class-documents.md:168-181`.\n\n**What a `.md` opening with `---` does today (all three verified):**\n1. **Render:** `remarkParse`+`remarkGfm` with no `remark-frontmatter` draws it as a thematic break plus a setext `<h2>title: x</h2>` — which then gets an autolink anchor and a TOC row the face's (frontmatter-skipping) heading list does not carry. No fixture in the vault has frontmatter, so `markdown/slugs.test.ts` never measures this divergence.\n2. **Face title:** `firstLine` (`format/src/documents.ts:329`) does not skip the block, so the sidebar/palette title is the literal `---` or the first YAML line.\n3. **Indexing:** `tagsIn`/`linksIn` scan the whole body including the block, so `#tag`-looking YAML values index as tags.\n\n**The shape of the fix** (per the brainstorm's ruling, needs its own ruling before a PR splits off):\n- `remark-frontmatter` in the browser pipeline, hidden from render (no phantom h2/hr, no TOC row).\n- `firstLine`/`tagsIn`/`linksIn` learn the same skip `headingsIn` already has.\n- Then the door the brainstorm names: surface YAML keys as document *properties*, so `prop:`/`has:`/`date:` stop selecting zero documents (the consequence pinned by `format/src/document.test.ts:72-79`).","created":"2026-08-20T17:17:45-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T19:53:31-04:00","custom":{"brainstorm":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md:168-181 — frontmatter ruled 'later' with the human 2026-08-19","from":"repo survey 2026-08-20 (Opus explore agent), on the human's ask"}}
{"id":"website","ord":"aJ","title":"Website: GitHub Pages at olai.kolu.dev","done":"2026-08-12T12:16:16-04:00","desc":"**Shipped in PR #123** (squash a8a0105, merged 2026-08-12T16:14:32Z) — authored and merged by the human directly, recorded here by the orchestrator after the fact.\n- A static landing page in the app's chalk palette (website/index.html, no build step)\n- CNAME olai.kolu.dev\n- Pages workflow deploying website/ on master pushes touching it\n\n**THE DOCS CONVENTION IT ESTABLISHES** (binding on all future PRs; relayed to the three in-flight agents at merge):\n- README.md is a POINTER (site + docs/index.md + HACKING.md) — future user-facing copy changes go to website/index.html\n- docs/ split into index.md, running.md, git.md, chat.md beside architecture.md and format.md\n- docs/git.md owns the git-integration story\n\n**One-time settings the human owns:**\n- Repo Pages source = GitHub Actions with the custom domain\n- Cloudflare CNAME olai → juspay.github.io\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:55-04:00"}
{"id":"website-refresh","parent":"website","ord":"a0","title":"Website refresh: six shipped PRs the site never heard about","done":"2026-08-13T11:13:42-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #137 (squash df23fe3, merged 2026-08-13).\n- The site caught up with #128–#133:\n  - A new Agenda section (predicate byte-for-byte with `agenda.ts`, the row picker, occurrences).\n  - Preferences with all fifteen palettes hex-for-hex as chips wearing their own colors.\n  - The mark walk as shipped (the ring corrected against `server/src/edit.ts` — done is not a stop; the author caught the brief's error).\n  - Chat file diffs.\n  - A swept `#format`/hero/daily.\n- **Grok review:** no MUST-FIX, accuracy verified against packages, both judgment calls accepted.\n  - Two NICE-TO-HAVEs taken in a final round (the daily-notes mock now shows scheduled and finished side by side — a day-page fact the site never had).\n- CI 10/10 Linux green at ddf0dea.\n- **Ruling honored:** the site describes MASTER; a depth touch-up follows only if/when depth merges.\n- HACKING.md's website/ checklist line keeps it current from here.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"inbox-count-placement","parent":"feat-nav","ord":"aE","title":"Inbox sits by Agenda and wears its count","done":"2026-08-21T08:23:25-04:00","desc":"The human, 2026-08-20 ~21:0x (screenshot ruling): the Inbox door (#297: above Trash, at the sidebar's bottom shelf) should (1) carry a COUNT of what's in the inbox, (2) sit CLOSE TO 'Agenda' rather than down by Trash, and (3) be consistently styled with the rest of the chrome re: count badge and colour — Agenda's badge is the reference. Grok lane; opencode debates; auto-merge on visual evidence.\n\n**pr** — the door beside Agenda, the count in Agenda's own chip (layout/chip.ts), hidden at zero\n\n**merge** — pre-approved after visual evidence","created":"2026-08-20T20:36:54-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:00:40-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-20","merge":"merge-human","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/28bf6880","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/308"}}
