{"id":"feat-orch","ord":"aI","title":"Orchestrator","desc":"The orchestrator, as a product of olai itself (the plan: [orchestrator.md](../brainstorming/orchestrator.md) rev 2 — olai is the harness ON TOP of kolu, never launches agents). The PR order is EDGES the board enforces (`set_doing` refuses a blocked phase), not prose. **The standing rule: each PR is complete and correct on its own the day it merges — nothing deferred; the phases sequence work, never split a feature into a broken half and its fix.** The Kolu child subtree groups the padi/fleet integration family.","created":"2026-08-21T13:00:39-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T10:43:10-04:00"}
{"id":"tool-elapsed-face","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aC","title":"PR: a tool call still running after a few seconds shows its elapsed time","done":"2026-08-21T17:19:05-04:00","desc":"- Any tool frame still `pending`/`in_progress` after ~N seconds, while the turn is live, gets elapsed time on its rail — \"· 47s\", ticking.\n- **Agent-agnostic by construction**: reads only ACP's own tool-call status plus whether a turn is in flight — no adapter `_meta`, no tool names — so it works with any ACP agent, not just the pinned Claude adapter.\n- Covers Monitor watchers, slow greps, long builds — anything the wire honestly calls running — with no need to recognize the tool.\n- Pattern: a pure sibling of `chat/spawn.ts`'s `doingOf` (PR #214's precedent), drawn from the same `Transcript.tsx` hook, unit-testable without starting an agent. Must gate on the conversation being live for `spawn.ts`'s own reason: statuses are sticky, and a dead conversation must not keep a timer counting.\n- Honest limit: this shows only what the wire calls running. Background calls the adapter completes at launch (background Task/Bash, likely Monitor) stay invisible until the adapter keeps them open — that half is upstream (claude-agent-acp issue #865; PR #941 covers Agent/Task only).\n\n**pr** — the elapsed rail off ACP status + liveness alone, per-row wake rule, clock.ts consolidation; the ChatEntry union question filed as chatentry-kind-union from=#324","created":"2026-08-21T15:23:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T17:19:05-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21, from the ACP subagent-display discussion","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/f4e657ba","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/324"}}
{"id":"quick-capture-door","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"aB","title":"PR: quick capture — POST /capture lands text in the inbox (Raycast, share sheet)","done":"2026-08-21T21:13:59-04:00","desc":"One small HTTP endpoint makes olai capturable from anywhere on the tailnet; every client after that is somebody else's few lines.\n\n**Ruled with the human 2026-08-21 (question tool):** v1 is TEXT-ONLY · auth is the tailscale identity header alone · every capture lands in the inbox · file capture is the follow-up node (capture-files).\n\n**The door:** `POST /capture` takes title/text/url, implemented over the same ops layer as everything else — validation, the inbox convention (`_olai/Inbox.olai`), auto-commit. Attribution: `Tailscale-User-Login` is required and recorded (tailscale serve injects it; transport is tailnet-gated, no public exposure, no token, no secret in any client). Captures arrive dated, so they land on the day's journal page. No `target` parameter in v1 — refile in the app; additive later.\n\n**Clients:**\n- **Raycast (macOS)** — the mail case with no mail infrastructure: AppleScript asks Mail.app for the selected message (Message-ID, subject, sender), builds the `message://…` link, prompts for a comment, POSTs. The link IS the attachment — the mail stays in Mail; olai holds the pointer, the comment, and `from`/`message-id` props (dedup via `prop:message-id`).\n- **Apple Shortcuts (iOS + macOS share sheet)** — URLs, selected text; \"Get Article using Safari Reader\" gives a read-later pipeline (article text as the note or a .md document).\n- Later, same endpoint: browser bookmarklet, Android via the PWA's Web Share Target, curl from scripts.\n\n**Two riders in this PR (verified against the code):**\n1. `message:` joins the sanitize schema — sanitise.ts is rehype-sanitize's default plus one named addition, and the default's href protocols are http/https/mailto, so a `message://` link in a note is STRIPPED today. One named protocol addition; sanitise.test.ts holds it against the default.\n2. Pin that the router hands non-http(s) hrefs to the OS instead of routing them, so a click opens Mail.app.\n\n**Caveats on the record:** `message:` links are solid on macOS; on iOS third-party-composed ones don't always resolve — subject/sender in the note keep captures findable regardless; test once. The retired alternative: an IMAP-folder-polling sidecar — only worth revisiting if full-body/attachment archiving is ever wanted (the vault outliving the mailbox).\n\n**pr** — POST /capture as a fourth Writer over the ops layer, CSRF closed under the serve threat model (strict content-type + Sec-Fetch-Site, pinned with proxy-supplied identity), both message:// riders, the palette/pin race folded via resolving.ts","see":["inbox-under-olai-dir","inbox-count-placement"],"created":"2026-08-21T16:47:29-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:08:28-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21, from the email-forwarding discussion","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/e9e62d23","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/327","superseded-by-354":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: POST /capture was RETIRED by #354 (\"POST /capture is gone\", running.md:294) — capture is now an /mcp verb reached by `olai surface --url … capture` (title+note); this node's body shape and Tailscale-User-Login requirement describe a door that no longer exists"}}
{"id":"duration-values","parent":"search","ord":"aD","title":"PR: the query grammar learns durations — created:1h, changed:30m (m/h/d/w)","done":"2026-08-21T18:48:39-04:00","desc":"The stamps carry second precision; the operators bottom out at days. One new value kind fixes it, RULED as follows.\n\n**The grammar:** durations spelled `<n><unit>`, units `m` (minutes), `h` (hours), `d` (days), `w` (weeks) — and NO month/year units ever (kills the Gmail-vs-Jira `m` collision by fiat, minutes win; month/year recency is already words: `last-month..`, `2026`). Two readings, both via the ranges the grammar already owns:\n- bare duration = within the last N (`created:1h`, sugar for `created:1h..`) — the Workflowy `last-changed:1h` / Gmail `newer_than:` reading, the one the human's fingers assumed;\n- duration as a range end = the point now−N (`created:..1h` is older-than-an-hour; `changed:2h..30m` a window; ends mix freely with day-words: `created:yesterday..3h`). Inequalities stay spelled as ranges — no `>=`, no `now-`.\n\n**Uniform across all three operators** (`date:`/`created:`/`changed:`): one value grammar, one refusal text; day-granular fields compare at their own precision, so `date:1h` effectively selects done-instants — stated in docs, not special-cased.\n\n**Anchoring:** ask-time, as `today`/`last-week` already are; a live `created:1h` page drifts within the hour exactly as `created:today` already drifts across midnight — evaluated at ask and on every revision, NO re-ask timer in v1.\n\n**Examples:** `created:1h` · `changed:30m` · `created:..1h` (older than an hour) · `changed:2h..30m` · `created:1d` vs `created:today` (rolling 24h vs since midnight) · `changed:1w` vs `changed:this-week` (rolling vs Monday-anchored) · `-changed:1d` (untouched a day) · `is:todo changed:1h`.\n\n**One place implements it:** the value grammar at the dates.ts/filter.ts boundary in @olai/format — the one-matcher rule means the palette, header box, on-page filter, chat @ list, ops search and MCP all inherit simultaneously. **Moves with it:** the refusal/usage text in filter.ts (the popover), search.md, filter-in-place.md's operator table, the search_nodes tool description.\n\n**Deliberately out:** comparison operators, snapping/rounding (`@h`, `/d`), function forms (`ago()`, `now-`), natural language, month/year duration units.\n\nPrior art surveyed 2026-08-21 (eleven systems; Workflowy the nearest kin — `last-changed:1h/1d`, hours+days only, bare = within-last-N): full survey in this node's git history via the removed brainstorming/relative-time-queries.md.\n\n**pr** — durations at the one-matcher boundary, hot path cheaper than before the feature, the refusal popover now teaches the grammar the human was refused by this afternoon","created":"2026-08-21T17:21:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T18:48:39-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21 — born from typing created:1h and being refused; the three design questions ruled via the question tool; the brainstorming doc folded into this node and removed on the human's order","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/f2251cce","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/328"}}
{"id":"feat-teams","ord":"aIV","title":"Teams","desc":"Using olai together over a tailnet: knowing who you are, choosing which agent you talk to, capture with attribution. Still to design when it hurts: several people writing on one branch (fetch, merge policy, whose-work-is-whose) — the old deferral was folded into this theme.","created":"2026-08-21T17:50:52-04:00"}
{"id":"opencode-chat","parent":"feat-teams","ord":"a0","title":"Opencode joins the chat: choose an agent per conversation","desc":"Design: brainstorming/opencode-chat.md (spike-verified against opencode 1.17.9 on this machine; rulings 2026-08-21).\n- Each conversation is bound to ONE agent, chosen when the chat is created (always ask). Group chat is out of scope, permanently.\n- The roster is auto-detected on the backend (PATH probe per known agent); an empty roster shows install instructions.\n- The header shows the agent's icon and name beside the model (bundled brand icons, generic fallback).\n- Two self-sufficient PRs below — nothing unused, nothing deferred.","created":"2026-08-21T17:50:52-04:00","custom":{"brainstorm":"brainstorming/opencode-chat.md","from":"the human 2026-08-21"}}
{"id":"opencode-pr1","parent":"opencode-chat","ord":"a0","title":"PR: fix the chat client's fragile ACP assumptions","done":"2026-08-22T01:50:32-04:00","desc":"Bugs today against ANY ACP agent — opencode just happens to trigger them — so this PR doesn't mention opencode at all:\n- Receiving the same tool_call_update twice must not break anything (opencode sends exact duplicates).\n- Stop using a frame's title as the tool's name — the title changes over a call's life; pick the name once at announcement.\n- A session/prompt that answers with an error (instead of a normal stop) must not wedge the conversation.\n- A replayed session that opens with user_message_chunk and already-collapsed tool frames must render fine.\nTested with the scripted fake agent the e2e suite already uses. Useful even if opencode support never lands.\n\n**pr** — the five any-agent robustness fixes incl. the ruled refused face (Unopened.tsx/face.ts), each pin mutation-checked; the chat panel stops betting on one agent's habits","created":"2026-08-21T17:50:52-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T01:50:32-04:00","custom":{"merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/cea1d914","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/331"}}
{"id":"opencode-pr2","parent":"opencode-pr1","ord":"a0","title":"PR: choosing an agent — roster detection, picker, header identity, the opencode leg #next","done":"2026-08-22T01:50:32-04:00","desc":"One PR, because no piece of it works without the others:\n- The server detects which agents are installed (PATH probe) and sends the client the list.\n- A new chat always asks which agent; an empty list shows install instructions instead.\n- The header shows the chosen agent's icon and name beside the model.\n- A conversation remembers its agent (stored next to its session id), so reopening it talks to the right one.\n- The opencode interpretation file: tool names from the toolCallId prefix, MCP auto-allow matches `<server>_`, no steering (the composer says messages will queue), settings read from method responses. The fail-safe rule stays: nothing is ever approved by failing to recognize it.\n- A fake opencode-shaped agent joins the e2e suite so all of the above is pinned.\nDetails and verified wire facts: brainstorming/opencode-chat.md.\n\n**pr** — @olai/chat agents/ legs (claude, opencode) behind one interface, roster detection (OLAI_ACP_AGENT + PATH probe, OLAI_AGENT_PATH), picker when >1 agent, header mark+name, the note remembers the agent, fail-safe shared, turn model a set (turns.ts) — which found and fixed a real idle-over-a-live-turn bug; 3 assumptions for the human: ask only when >1 installed (narrows 'always ask'), choose-at-boot adopts, memory one conversation deep","after":["opencode-pr1"],"created":"2026-08-21T17:50:52-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T01:50:32-04:00","custom":{"merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/3bf9ce9f","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/336"}}
{"id":"tailscale-identity","parent":"feat-teams","ord":"a1","title":"PR: the header shows who you are — a trusted identity header (tailscale serve, Caddy + OAuth), with gravatar","done":"2026-08-21T20:50:31-04:00","desc":"- One configurable pair of trusted header names (login + optional email) tells olai who the signed-in person is; the reverse proxy in front injects them. Default wiring: tailscale serve's `Tailscale-User-Login`. The same config covers Caddy + GitHub OAuth (caddy-security's `X-Token-User-*` via `inject headers with claims`, or forward_auth → oauth2-proxy's `X-Auth-Request-User`/`-Email`) and Authelia/Pomerium (`Remote-User`/`Remote-Email`) — one feature, not one per proxy.\n- The header shows the person: gravatar from the hashed email (generic fallback when no email claim), name beside or on hover.\n- The same value is the attribution other features read — /capture (quick-capture-door's ruling) and, later, whose-work-is-whose in team use.\n- No header (direct access, dev) → no identity chip, nothing breaks.\n- **Trust rule, stated in the PR**: the header is only meaningful when the proxy is the only way in — olai bound to loopback/tailnet, and the proxy stripping client-supplied copies of the header. Document it beside the config.\n- **Probable kolu ask**: the app is a websocket, so the header must be read at upgrade time — kolu's `serveSurfaceApp` owns the upgrade and doesn't hand request headers to the app today; exposing selected headers to the connection context is likely a small upstream change. Plain HTTP endpoints (the future /capture) read headers directly, no kolu change.\n- Implementation note: gravatar is a remote image fetch from gravatar.com — make sure the app page allows that image origin.\n\n**pr** — (by the human) — @olai/identity, GET /olai/who, the chip with honest absence, one config for Tailscale/Caddy/Authelia; the kolu websocket ask lives on as kolu-upgrade-headers in the Inbox","created":"2026-08-21T17:50:52-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T20:50:31-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/c4366b9b","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/330"}}
{"id":"identity-avatar-ladder","parent":"feat-teams","ord":"a2","title":"PR: the identity chip stops assuming the login is an email — real avatars for Tailscale and GitHub #next","done":"2026-08-22T01:02:29-04:00","desc":"Follow-up to #330, from its first real deployment.\n\n**The motivating case:** a GitHub-backed tailnet's `Tailscale-User-Login` is `srid@github` — Tailscale's own spelling, correct to display, but NOT an email. #330 assumes login = email (\"that header is the email\", docs/running.md), so the gravatar hashes a non-address and every GitHub- or passkey-backed tailscale account gets the generic silhouette forever.\n\n**Fix — a picture resolution ladder, one config family, no provider hardcoding:**\n1. A **picture header**, when the proxy sends one (new optional `OLAI_IDENTITY_PICTURE_HEADER`; tailscale serve injects `Tailscale-User-Profile-Pic` — the IdP's real avatar, e.g. the GitHub one). Also read `Tailscale-User-Name` (display name) via an optional name header.\n2. An **avatar URL template** (`OLAI_IDENTITY_AVATAR_TEMPLATE`, e.g. `https://github.com/{login}.png`) — this is the Caddy + GitHub OAuth answer: oauth2-proxy's `X-Auth-Request-User` is the GitHub username, and GitHub serves every user's avatar unauthenticated at that URL. No API, no token.\n3. **Gravatar from the email claim** — only when the value actually looks like an email; #330's behavior, demoted to fallback.\n4. The generic silhouette.\n\n**Also in this PR:** correct docs/running.md's login-is-the-email claim (true for Google/Microsoft/Okta tailnets, false for GitHub/passkey ones), and the per-proxy wiring table gains the picture/name/template columns.\n\n**pr** — picture ladder (picture header → avatar template → gravatar-if-email → silhouette) resolved server-side, name header, /olai/who {login,name,picture}, img-src 'self' blob: https:, running.md corrected + proxy table; 3 assumptions for the human: Tailscale default header names (non-tailscale proxies must empty them — documented), https:-only rungs, tooltip name+login","see":["tailscale-identity"],"created":"2026-08-21T20:59:33-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T01:02:29-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21, on deploying #330 (the srid@github confusion)","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/3d45ff08","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/337"}}
{"id":"vault-level-settings","parent":"feat-teams","ord":"a3","title":"PR: CLI/nix can pin git policy — the Prefs toggles freeze read-only when it does #next","done":"2026-08-21T23:45:41-04:00","desc":"**The problem:** in a team deployment, auto-commit/auto-push must be the server's decision, the same for everyone — not whichever browser's pref happens to be set. Single-user, today's browser prefs are fine and stay.\n\n**Ruled 2026-08-21 (refined the same day):**\n- **Default: unchanged.** With no flag given, \"Git commit\" and \"Git push\" remain live browser prefs exactly as they are today.\n- **The override: CLI flags** (`--commit`, `--push`), surfaced as home-manager module options. When a flag is given, the server tells the client, and the Prefs toggles render in the pinned state, **read-only, with the source named** (\"set by the server: --commit=auto\"). Never hidden, never overridable from a browser.\n- **No vault settings file** (the earlier settings.json / Settings.olai brainstorm is dissolved): policy is a property of the running instance, and a file in the vault would make a personal clone inherit the team's auto-push via `git pull` — exactly wrong.\n- The refusal-pause behavior survives under a pin as runtime STATE: a refused commit/push still pauses the loop, and the frozen section carries a **Resume** button (today's off-and-back-on dance needs a live toggle, which a pinned section no longer has).\n- Theme/font/size/notes/done/hidden-outlines are untouched — personal view choices, per-browser.\n\n**Ships:** the two flags + HM options, the pin traveling to the client, the frozen faces with their sentence, Resume, docs/running.md.\n\n**pr** — --commit/--push as a pin on the git cell, Prefs rows frozen with the flag named, Resume under a pin, HM services.olai.commit/.push; 3 assumptions for the human: --push governs browsers only (no server-side push), --commit auto→on/manual→off/off→off, --no-commit pins as --commit=off","created":"2026-08-21T21:03:26-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T23:45:41-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21, from the Prefs screenshot review","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/524e9086","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/335"}}
{"id":"one-search-box","parent":"search","ord":"aE","title":"PR: one search box — in the HEADER on every page, scoped to the page by a deletable \"This page\" chip, searching everywhere (/search?q=…) without it; the page filter bar and ⌘K's node hits go #next","todo":true,"desc":"**The complaint (2026-08-21):** `#next` was tagged on five nodes in three outlines and nothing in the app lists them together. The filter box, `?q=`, and clicking a tag all narrow ONE page; the only directory-wide doors (header box, ⌘K) are shortlists for jumping TO a node — capped at 8, no address, not pinnable. Two entry points, two scopes, two answer shapes, one grammar.\n\n**Ruled (question tool, 2026-08-21):**\n1. **One box survives: the page's filter box.** It already owns the address (`?q=`), the honest \"N of M\" count, ancestry-kept rows, the refusal line and pins. The header's search box is deleted; on the phone the magnifier focuses the one box.\n2. **Page first, widen explicitly.** Typing narrows the page in front of you exactly as today. The bar gains the missing truth beside \"3 of 41\": how many matched **elsewhere in the directory** (\"· 12 more in other files — search everywhere\"), and that line is the door that widens the SAME query. A shortcut for it is welcome (design to pick — e.g. Enter with nothing selected, or a scope toggle on the bar); the query text is never retyped.\n3. **Everywhere is a real page: `/search?q=…`** — a computed page beside /today, /agenda, /trash in routes.ts (spells no file; the one-page rule and `is:trashed` apply as on any door). Rows grouped by file, each with its ancestry kept and its reason lit (the filter's \"every row says why\"), uncapped, with its own \"N matches in K files\" count. Addressable, back-button, and **pinnable like any `?q=` page** — so a saved cross-vault search is a pin (`/search?q=%23next`). From a row, Enter/click goes to the node; the page is the thing the shortlist could never be.\n4. **⌘K focuses the one box.** The palette keeps its commands, the page's verbs and the pin row; its node-hit half goes — a non-command query hands off to the one box (on the current page, with the widen line). The `LIMIT = 8` shortlist (`search/Shortlist.tsx`, `count.ts`) and `HeaderSearch.tsx` are deleted, not kept as a preview; the composer's `@` list (chat) keeps its own bounded shortlist — it names one node into a message and is not a search door.\n\n**Consequences to carry, not re-decide:** one matcher still (`@olai/format` parseFilter/matching; the server answers every door — the page asks `Query.search` uncapped-or-paged, the in-place narrowing keeps riding the page's revision pulse per filter-rides-the-page.md). The \"more elsewhere\" number must be the wire's uncapped `total` minus the page's matches, or a second ask with no `file`/`under` scope — never a browser walk (vault-in-browser). Documents are hits on the everywhere page (search.md \"…and documents\"); they are not rows on a page filter today and that stays.\n\n**Design first, in the PR:** a short `docs/brainstorming/one-search-box.md` (the widen gesture, the row shape on /search, what the bar says at each scope, mobile) lands as the PR's first commit for the human to read before the code; docs/search.md's \"five doors\" paragraph becomes the one-door story.\n\n**pr** — CLOSED unmerged 2026-08-22 on the human's word — the UI to be re-evaluated later; branch one-search-box on origin holds both rounds (page-filter design at acdb4ee; header-box + This-page-chip round after)","created":"2026-08-21T21:48:57-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T08:35:08-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21 — tagged #next across three files and found no page that shows them all; the four rulings taken by the question tool the same evening","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/334","ruled-2026-08-22":"THE HUMAN, on reviewing #334 (~07:55): 'The one search box should be in the HEADER. Simple as. Exists in all pages. On .olai pages, it gets a \"This page\" thing by default (which the user can delete) to filter.' — this supersedes the earlier reading that the page's filter box survives; the box is the header's, on every page, with scope as a deletable chip; deleting the chip searches everywhere (/search?q=), re-adding it scopes to the page; ⌘K focuses that box. #334 is being rebuilt to it (lane-osb, address round 2).","ruled-2026-08-22-cmdk":"THE HUMAN ~08:37: 'I don't want to lose the Cmd+K palette UI' — the ⌘K palette stays as on master (commands, verbs, pins; its handoff rows into the one box are fine); ⌘K is NOT rebound to the header box. Supersedes the 'focuses the one box' reading of ruling 4 and the orchestrator's round-2 brief item 4.","status-2026-08-22":"back to todo; no design is ruled — the human re-evaluates the UI; what IS settled: one matcher, /search?q= as a real page was built and reviewed clean, the ⌘K palette UI stays","touches":"web/src/client/filter (FilterBar, narrowed, count), search (HeaderSearch, Shortlist, nodes LIMIT=8, count), palette (items, Palette), routes.ts (a computed page), pins; docs/search.md, editing.md; website"}}
{"id":"mcp-roster-visible","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aD","title":"PR: the chat shows which MCP servers a conversation has, not just the failures","done":"2026-08-23T20:27:17-04:00","desc":"- #140 (mcp-fail-visible) shows MCP FAILURES in a strip and deliberately nothing on a healthy session. But \"which servers does this conversation have?\" is a question people actually ask — and the motivating incident is the model answering it wrong (opencode listed olai and deepwiki, omitted kolu, then called `kolu_lifecycle_create` successfully). The UI should answer it, not the model.\n\n**What to draw, honest per layer:**\n- **Handed by olai** (fully knowable, already computed by #140's probe + the `servers` event on the chat cell): `olai` (its own HTTP route, alive by construction) and `kolu` (probe-verified at session open). Chips with a dot — `olai ✓ · kolu ✓` — in the chat header popover, or the #140 strip generalized into the roster with per-server state (failures keep their verbatim sentences).\n- **Actually connected, where the agent says so**: the Claude adapter's `_claude/sdkMessage` system-init carries per-MCP-server connection status — one more field read from the same message the live model already comes from (claude leg only).\n- **The agent's own servers** (e.g. deepwiki from the user's opencode.json): invisible to olai by construction — say \"plus the agent's own\", never pretend the list is complete.\n\n**Scope note:** the display is per-conversation (servers are handed at session open); the roster row lives with the agent identity the header already shows.\n\n**pr** — 2026-08-23 20:26 on the human's approval — the roster off the literal mcpServers array, connected minted only from the claude leg's init (verbatim word, sessionId-guarded), agent's-own servers honestly row-less behind \"plus the agent's own\" (both reviewers engaged and agreed), refusedOpen/wentAway clear the strip, #140's failure sentences intact; darwin CI lane fully green on quiet petit, Linux red only on the load-flake legs (Inbox-filed); evidence: six images + unopened before/after pair","see":["mcp-fail-visible"],"created":"2026-08-22T12:30:24-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T20:27:20-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22 — asked opencode \"what MCPs do you have\" and it omitted kolu, then used kolu fine","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/4108cf9b","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/357"}}
{"id":"git-policy-server-side","parent":"feat-git","ord":"a4","title":"Git policy moves to the server: Auto-commit's quiet-window loop, Auto-push, the pause and the outcome are facts about the directory, not one tab's memory #now","done":"2026-08-22T17:20:31-04:00","desc":"**Today:** Auto-commit (#301) is a 15 s quiet-window loop in the browser (commit/auto.ts, flurry.ts) behind a per-browser Web-Locks leader (commit/elected.ts); Auto-push (#283) fires only after THIS tab's commit (commit/record.ts:26); the pause-on-refusal (commit/pause.ts) and the last commit/push outcome (commit/state.ts) are tab memory. The server's `--commit=auto` is a different thing (one commit per write, no window, never pushed — `gitPolicy.ts:82`). #335 called the browser-preference shape \"exactly wrong for a team\" and answered by PINNING the toggles, not by moving the loop.\n\n**Ruled (the human):** git policy is a fact about the DIRECTORY. The loop lives on the server (one per served directory; quiet window over the server's own `pending`, which MCP/capture/vim writes move too); `--push=auto` pushes after each settled commit — the server's own included; the refusal, the pause and the last push outcome are fields of the git cell, drawn on the chip (⚠ with git's words, never `✓ committed` over a failing push) and identical in every tab; the prefs toggles set the server's policy through a procedure, persisted outside the vault (no settings file that travels with `git pull` — #335 stands), pinned by the flags when given; the tab loop, leader lock, tab pause and per-tab outcome signals are deleted.\n\n**Why browser-side happened:** the quiet window was framed as \"the person stopped typing\" — a claim about the reader — and shipped as a prefs row beside theme; nobody built the server-side window. The other browser-side residents are fine (theme, density, Done-visibility, panel geometry, folds, undo, chat drafts) — the git family is the whole of the nonsense.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as bec4334c","created":"2026-08-22T13:36:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T17:20:31-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22 13:35, after the push-failure RCA: 'why was auto-commit browser-side? any other nonsense riding browser-side?' — ruled: move it server-side, dispatch to Opus, auto-merge on verification","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/349","ruled-restart":"the human 17:05: remember nothing across a restart; under --push=auto with unpushed commits, one push on boot re-earns the words; nothing under manual/off"}}
{"id":"push-failure-invisible","parent":"git-policy-server-side","ord":"a0","title":"A refused push is invisible: the chip says \"✓ committed · 13 unpushed\" and nothing tells you why — the push outcome lives only in one tab's memory #now","done":"2026-08-22T17:20:30-04:00","desc":"**Symptom:** auto-push on; the header chip reads `✓ committed · 1h ago · 13 unpushed`, the popover \"13 commits not on origin/main · Push\" — and no error anywhere.\n\n**Root cause (two facts, both by design today):**\n1. **Auto-push is a browser behaviour, not a server one.** The only trigger is `packages/web/src/client/commit/record.ts:26` — `if (autoPush && tag === \"Committed\") push()` — inside the success callback of THIS tab's own `git.commit` (Commit button or this tab's Auto-commit loop). Commits made by `--commit=auto` on the server, by an agent's `commit` tool, or by `POST /capture` are never pushed (`packages/ops/src/pending.ts:819-891` ends without a push; `docs/running.md:207`, `docs/git.md:95` say so). So \"unpushed\" grows whenever the writer was not a browser tab.\n2. **A push refusal is never stored.** `packages/git/src/git.ts:803` runs a bare `git push` (no hard-coded branch — `origin/main` is parsed from `git status --branch`, `git.ts:509-517`; `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` + 10 s budget, so no hang); a refusal is `Effect.logWarning(\"olai git: the branch was not pushed\", said)` and returned to the one caller (`pending.ts:785-790`), which does NOT call `settled()` / `onRecorded` — so the `git` cell (`GitState = {status, said, pinned}`, `packages/format/src/committing.ts:142-165`) has no push-error field and is not republished. The only place the words exist is the per-tab signal `pushed` (`commit/state.ts:132`), cleared on the next attempt (`:142`), lost on reload, drawn only inside the popover (`Unpushed.tsx:62-68`), never on the chip (`said.ts:289` has no push arm). Auto-commit's pause on a failed push (`auto.ts:194-198`) is also in-memory per tab.\n\n**Other ways it reads green while failing:** the server pin `--push=off` silently overrides the browser toggle (`settings/autopush.ts:36`; the prefs row shows \"Set by the server\" — easy to miss); `--commit=off` disables push too (`pending.ts:764`); a non-fast-forward because origin/main moved (olai never pulls/rebases) refuses every push forever.\n\n**Fix (the seam):**\n- `pending.ts`: keep a `pushRefusal` beside `refusal` (`:424`), set on the Failed arm (`:786`), cleared on a successful push (`:792`), and call `options.onRecorded?.()` on failure too so the cell republishes.\n- `format/committing.ts`: `GitState` gains `pushSaid: NullOr(String)` (`sameGit` is schema-derived, picks it up).\n- Chip: `said.ts:324-327` `alsoUnpushed` says `· 13 unpushed — the last push was refused: <said>` when set, and `faceOf`/`Commit.tsx:117-120` shows a ⚠ face instead of `✓ committed` while a push is failing; the popover reads the cell, not only the tab-local signal.\n- And decide the first fact: should `--push=auto` also push the server's own `--commit=auto` commits (one network round trip per quiet window, not per write)? Today's docs say no; the symptom says a user with auto-push on expects yes.\n\n**Confirm on an instance:** `journalctl --user -u olai --since -3h | grep 'olai git:'` — `the branch was not pushed` + git's stderr is the only durable record; its absence means no push was attempted. `git log origin/main..HEAD --format='%s%n%(trailers:key=X-Olai-Writer)'` shows who made the 13.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as bec4334c (pushSaid on the git cell; the chip drops ✓ and carries git's words; a boot push under --push=auto re-earns the words after a restart)","created":"2026-08-22T13:24:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T17:20:30-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22 13:20 (screenshot: committed 1h ago · 13 unpushed on origin/main, auto-push on, no feedback); RCA by the orchestrator's explorer","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/349"}}
{"id":"surface-cli","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"aD","title":"`olai surface`: a CLI for every server verb, over HTTP","done":"2026-08-23T16:44:01-04:00","desc":"**What this is.** One command, `olai surface <verb>`, that can call any verb the server offers (the same verbs MCP agents see, same names, same answers) from a terminal or a script. The generic part lives in kolu (`@kolu/surface-cli`, merged as kolu#2205); olai adds its verbs, the `capture` verb, and how to reach a running olai.\n\n**Decided 2026-08-23 (replaces the unix-socket design of #352, reverted):**\n- The CLI reaches the server over **HTTP**, exactly as `/mcp` does. No unix socket. `--url <server>` is required on every call — no default, no lookup.\n- Auth: the `/mcp` bearer locally; the reverse proxy's identity header remotely. `captured-by` = that identity header, or omitted. A caller can never set it.\n- A write prints one line — `captured into <vault> — <link>`; `--json` prints the full answer, which names the vault (root path + server URL). No magic on TTY.\n- `capture` takes a title and a note, nothing else, for now.\n- `olai surface` prints friendly help; the help is the doc.\n\n**Still true from 2026-08-22:** no phone door (phones use the web page); flat verb names identical to MCP; no `olai mcp` subcommand; `capture` is one entry in the TOOLS table so the CLI verb and the MCP tool are the same line; `POST /capture` goes once `olai surface --url … capture` is proven against the human's real vault.\n\n**History.** #352 shipped this over a per-user unix socket — unapproved; two servers on one machine raced for it and the human's capture landed in this repo's docs vault; a vault in a container behind HTTPS was unreachable. Merged without approval 2026-08-23, reverted the same day (#353), re-opened as draft #354. Nothing here merges without the human's explicit approval.\n\nDesign doc: brainstorming/surface-cli.md (rev 2 — to be revised to HTTP).","see":["quick-capture-door","surface-mcp"],"created":"2026-08-22T15:49:19-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T16:44:01-04:00","custom":{"brainstorm":"brainstorming/surface-cli.md — rev 2 carries the rulings: Effect CLI assumed, no phone door, captured-by = what the door has, flat names, no olai mcp","from":"the human 2026-08-22, after /capture (#327): 'bad solution — we need a surface CLI client that can call any surface verb; just like surface-mcp, upstream surface-cli'","post-merge-bugs":"2026-08-23 12:05-12:20, the human on master after #352 (merged by the orchestrator without the human's approval): six child nodes (docs, wrong-vault, remote-capture, runtime-dir-flood, socket-mode-claim, exit-0-no-root). 12:18 RULED: surface.sock was an unapproved decision — #352 REVERTED (#353 = df841d7c, 12:25), re-opened as draft #354 from the same head for the follow-up; NOTHING in this area merges without the human's explicit approval.","shipped":"kolu#2205 merged 7a004a82 (2026-08-22); olai #352 merged 441b8f74 without approval and REVERTED (#353); now open: draft olai #354 + kolu#2207 (cli-override) — both to be taken to green with everything under this node, both approved by the human before merging"}}
{"id":"surface-cli-kolu","parent":"surface-cli","ord":"a0","title":"PR (kolu): `@kolu/surface-cli`","done":"2026-08-22T22:08:42-04:00","desc":"Three commits that each stand alone: (1) the move, no behaviour change — `packages/surface/src/verbs.ts` exporting `SurfaceVerb`, `toolName`, `toInputSchema`; surface-mcp re-exports the old names, its tests unchanged and green prove it. (2) `packages/surface-cli`: `surfaceCommands`, `flagsOf`, `EXIT`; no new dependency; tests drive the README's fixture surface (load / processes / proc.kill) over serveOverUnixSocket end-to-end — golden --help, every flag shape, get/keys/watch as ndjson, the exit matrix, Ctrl-C on --follow. kolu-cli is NOT migrated in this PR. (3) website `surface/expose-to-cli.mdx` + `ref-surface-cli`, package README, expose.ts's 'which faces take one' paragraph names the CLI. CI per the odu skill, Linux; note the merged SHA for the olai pin.\n\n**kolu-pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as 7a004a82 (via kolu's /be + /ci; Linux lane on localhost, darwin on ci@petit; 31 commits in the three parts)","created":"2026-08-22T15:49:19-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T12:23:14-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2205"}}
{"id":"surface-cli-olai","parent":"surface-cli","ord":"a1","title":"PR #354: the CLI talks HTTP to the server named by `--url` (required); the unix socket goes","done":"2026-08-23T16:43:50-04:00","desc":"Change on #354: replace the unix-socket transport with HTTP. Every `olai surface` call takes `--url <server>` — required, no default, no lookup of a remembered URL. The CLI is an MCP client of that server's `/mcp` (ruled 2026-08-23 12:52): one door, no new route; auth as `/mcp` clients do (loopback, else the bearer; through a reverse proxy the identity header). Streaming verbs (`get --follow`, `watch`) are not offered — `/mcp` is POST-only, accepted. `captured-by` = the identity header, else omitted; never caller-set. Delete `surface.sock`, `serveOverUnixSocket`, `--socket`, the dial ladder and their tests. POST /capture is deleted only after `olai surface --url https://myolai… capture` is shown working against the human's real vault (transcript in the PR).\n\nWhy: #352 used one unix socket per user — two servers on a machine raced for it and the human's capture landed in the wrong vault; a vault in a container behind HTTPS was unreachable.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-23 as 6a863f38 on the human's approval (CI green at the approved head e88e97c4; the video verified)","after":["surface-cli-kolu"],"created":"2026-08-22T15:49:19-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T16:43:50-04:00","custom":{"kolu-side":"anything #354 needs from kolu (the help layout; any HTTP-face plumbing) goes onto the open kolu#2207 branch (cli-override) — the human's standing rule 2026-08-23; #354 pins that branch's head until #2207 merges","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/354","ruled-2026-08-23":"HTTP like /mcp; remote over HTTPS with the identity header; captured-by = the header or omitted; human line + link on a terminal, JSON for scripts; old rulings (no phone door, flat names, no olai mcp, capture in TOOLS) stand; nothing merges without the human's approval","ruled-transport":"the human 2026-08-23 12:52 (question tool, on the author's stop-and-ask): the CLI becomes an MCP CLIENT at /mcp — literally one door, zero new exposure; kolu#2207 adds an MCP-client-backed SurfaceClientCallable; no new olai route. Cost accepted: `get --follow` / `watch` are gone (no streaming over /mcp)."}}
{"id":"surface-cli-docs","parent":"surface-cli","ord":"a2","title":"PR #354 (+ kolu#2207): `olai surface` prints friendly help text","done":"2026-08-23T16:43:50-04:00","desc":"Change: `olai surface` (and `--help`) prints help a person can read — a one-line purpose, the verbs grouped by what they do (read, search, write, capture) each with a one-line description and an example, `--url` and `--json`, where the answer goes. Today it dumps the raw generated verb table.\n\nThe help layout belongs to `@kolu/surface-cli` so every surface client gets it — build it there, on the open kolu#2207 branch (the human: use that PR, no new kolu PR), with olai supplying only its own wording (purpose line, groups, examples). No separate docs page; the help is the doc (README and running.md point at `olai surface --help`). A test pins the help text.\n\n**pr** — 6a863f38) — the help IS the doc; pinned by surfaceCli.test.ts's golden; kolu#2207 carries the layout","created":"2026-08-23T12:07:54-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T16:43:50-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-23 12:05 on master after #352: 'where the fuck are docs for the surface command?' — #352 was merged by the orchestrator on a misread approval; the human did NOT approve it","held":"the human approves the PR personally","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/354"}}
{"id":"surface-cli-remote-capture","parent":"surface-cli","ord":"a4","title":"PR #354: capture takes a title and a note, nothing else","done":"2026-08-23T16:43:51-04:00","desc":"Change on #354: `olai surface capture \"title\" --text \"note\"` — the link field (`--url`) and the free props go; `--url` means the server now. More fields can come later.\n\n**pr** — 6a863f38) — capture takes a title and --text; --url is the server; proven against the human's vault (row bjx3jlui)","created":"2026-08-23T12:12:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T16:43:51-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-23 12:08 — passed `--url https://myolai.rooster-blues.ts.net/` to capture (the capture's link field) almost certainly meaning 'capture INTO that olai'; #352 deleted POST /capture under ruling option 1 (ssh recipe) and the human now observes the loss on master","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/354","ruling-history":"2026-08-22 22:15 the human chose (1) ssh recipe over (2) a second AGENT websocket face behind the identity header over (3) keep POST /capture; the author had recommended (2) if the recipe must keep working"}}
{"id":"surface-socket-mode-claim","parent":"surface-cli","ord":"a6","title":"Bug: docs claimed a 0700 socket file (moot)","done":"2026-08-23T12:21:15-04:00","desc":"Moot: the unix socket is gone from the design (decided 2026-08-23). Kept as a record of what was wrong in #352.","created":"2026-08-23T12:12:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T12:23:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"orchestrator RCA 2026-08-23 12:15: `ls -la /run/user/1000/olai/surface.sock` → srwxr-xr-x; the directory /run/user/1000/olai is drwx------","where":"docs/running.md:265 'Auth is the socket's mode'; serve.ts:262-270 'a 0700 socket in a private directory'; kolu's serveOverUnixSocket sets the mode"}}
{"id":"surface-cli-exit-0-no-root","parent":"surface-cli","ord":"a7","title":"PR #354: a write prints one line and a link; `--json` for the full answer","done":"2026-08-23T16:43:52-04:00","desc":"Change on #354: a write prints `captured into <vault> — <link to the row>`. With `--json` it prints the JSON answer instead (which carries the vault root and server URL). No TTY detection — the flag decides. Applies to every write verb.\n\n**pr** — 6a863f38) — one line + row link; --json for the record","created":"2026-08-23T12:12:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T16:43:52-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human's transcript 2026-08-23 12:08 — the answer is the ops-layer WriteResult verbatim (id, title, file, summary, sort, captured, rev, why, did); nothing in it is a thing a person at a terminal can click or ls","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/354","where":"packages/server/src/main.ts (the bespoke verbs print the ops answer as JSON); docs/running.md:247-255 shows the same JSON as the documented experience"}}
{"id":"chat-background-tasks-visible","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aE","title":"PR: a background task the agent arms (Monitor) is visible in the chat panel","done":"2026-08-24T14:25:12-04:00","desc":"- The motivating incident: the orchestrator armed `kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m` as a persistent Monitor and supervised a whole dispatch off its events — and the chat panel showed none of it: no spawn, no event stream, no liveness, no death. The human had to ask \"how do you know you are babysitting right now?\"; the answer (pid, event cadence) lived only in prose.\n- **What to draw:** a background task gets a lane/row of its own (the chat-subagent-lanes precedent, #193): its description (\"kolu fleet watch…\"), armed-since, each event as it streams (these arrive as harness notifications between turns), and its END — exit code on death, since a monitor's death is precisely the fact the human must not miss. tool-elapsed-face (#324) already ticks elapsed time on anything the wire honestly calls running.\n- **The honest limit is upstream, and must be said per layer** (the mcp-roster-visible pattern): today nothing about a Monitor reaches the ACP wire as a running call, and its events arrive as system notifications inside later turns' context, not as session updates. Draw what the wire carries; where it carries nothing, this node's other half is the adapter ask — not a client-side guess.\n- **Upstream, verified 2026-08-23** — the repo is `agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp` (the pinned adapter; the zed-industries name redirects there):\n  - Issue #865 (OPEN, filed 2026-07-12): https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp/issues/865 — the launch tool result returns a `backgroundTaskId`, so the ACP `tool_call` reaches `completed` at LAUNCH; the adapter *receives* the real signals from the SDK stream and drops them (`case \"background_tasks_changed\": break;`, and `task_updated`/`task_notification` only prune an attribution map). Its proposal — forward `background_tasks_changed` as the full live set — is exactly what this node's lane would draw.\n  - PR #941 (OPEN, unmerged, 0 reviews): https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp/pull/941 — keeps async Agent/Task calls `in_progress` until a real terminal state, but by its own summary \"background Bash retain their existing behavior\" and it never touches `background_tasks_changed`. So Monitor/background Bash stay invisible even if it lands — and it has NOT landed, so today upstream covers nothing at all.\n  - No Monitor-specific issue exists upstream (a search finds only #603 — completion notifications blocking the query queue; adjacent, not this). The adapter ask — Monitor/background-Bash coverage, i.e. #865's full-live-set proposal — is unclaimed.\n- Scope note: per-conversation, like everything on the chat cell; a task outliving the pane's conversation is out of scope until the wire says otherwise.\n\n**pr** — 2026-08-24 14:26 — a background task the agent arms is its own live row AND lives on the fixed header strip while out (the second ruling), its death landing at the transcript's bottom with the exit code; the adapter half extends claude-agent-acp#941 via a pinned, README-audited patch (upstream issue #1038 asks about a PR); the evidence twice frame-verified by the orchestrator; CI 10/10 localhost","see":["tool-elapsed-face","chat-subagent-lanes"],"created":"2026-08-23T18:06:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T14:25:14-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-23 — watching the orchestrator session over ACP chat: the fleet-watch Monitor (kolu watch, the session's entire supervision spine) rendered nowhere; only the orchestrator's prose no-ops betrayed its existence","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/87a176eb","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/365","ruled":"the human 2026-08-23 ~17:45 (question tool): file under features → Chat panel","ruled-2":"the human 2026-08-24 12:52 (probing #365's built UX): a long-lived task's activity must not live only at its birth position in the transcript — while OUT it sits in the fixed header strip (the #357 roster precedent, visible regardless of scroll); on END the strip clears and a fresh row lands at the transcript's BOTTOM at that moment; the original tool row remains the arming's historical record"}}
{"id":"chat-attention-alerts","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aF","title":"PR: a sound + system notification when the chat awaits the human","done":"2026-08-23T21:09:39-04:00","desc":"**The UX, as agreed:**\n- When the agent is blocked on the human — a question form, a permission prompt, a plan approval (the states form-elicitation #110 made renderable) — and the pane is NOT focused: one short chime plus a system notification naming the conversation and the first line of what it wants. Clicking it focuses the right tab/pane, scrolled to the prompt.\n- When the pane IS focused: nothing — the form appearing is the alert; no nagging about what is already on screen.\n- A badge sticks until the human focuses the pane (not until the notification is dismissed): the App Badging API on the installed PWA icon, falling back to a title/favicon dot in a plain tab. ~~with the count of conversations awaiting~~ **As built (#358, grok NIT 2): the badge counts PENDING QUESTIONS in the one conversation the cell carries** — the only number available under this node's own no-new-wire rule; the docs say the number's meaning so a dock \"3\" is not read as three chats.\n- Turn-complete is deliberately silent (ruled): only awaiting-the-human alerts.\n\n**PWA-shaped (ruled — olai runs installed as a PWA):**\n- The notification goes through the service worker (`registration.showNotification`), so it fires with the app window backgrounded; notification click routes focus through the SW's clients. **As built: the seam is `@kolu/surface-app/notify` (a fetch-less notification worker served at `/sw.js`); the chime is two Web Audio oscillators, no dependency.**\n- One-time browser permission ask on first enable; if denied, chime + badge still work (neither needs permission). **As built: plus an \"Allow notifications\" button for browsers that refuse a background ask; the denied path is scenario-pinned (grok SHOULD 3).**\n- **Honest limit:** no push server in v1 — the trigger is the live websocket, so alerts fire while the app runs (foreground or background). A fully-closed PWA hears nothing; Web Push (a push service, subscriptions, a server key) is its own node if ever wanted.\n\n**Default ON** (ruled), with Prefs toggles: alerts on/off, sound on/off — beside the chat's existing prefs. **As built: the sound row goes inert, not hidden, while alerts are off.**\n\n**Scope note:** the \"awaiting\" fact must come from the chat cell's own state (the pending form/permission the panel already renders), not from a new wire signal — the panel knows it is drawing a form nobody has answered.\n\n**Review deltas folded (#358 address round):** a one-bit cross-tab \"origin is watched\" broadcast so a second same-vault tab never chimes while the focused tab shows the form (grok SHOULD 1); the notification press stays \"asked\" until hydration delivers values, so a press during load cannot be spent as jump-to-bottom (SHOULD 2); the e2e press sends the production envelope (id + source), not the no-id fallback (SHOULD 4).\n\n**pr** — 2026-08-23 21:10 — chime + SW notification + badge only when the agent awaits you, silent when watched anywhere (cross-tab claim), press survives hydration, denied permission leaves chime+badge (pinned), badge counts questions and says so; CI 10/10 x86_64-linux at 2231148f; evidence video frame-verified by the orchestrator per the human's condition","see":["form-elicitation"],"created":"2026-08-23T18:12:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T21:09:41-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-23 — \"I want notification alerts (with sound) whenever chat needs my attention (like question prompts)\"","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/5160e9e4","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/358","ruled":"the human 2026-08-23 ~18:15 (question tool): trigger = only when the agent awaits the human (turn-complete stays silent); channel = PWA-shaped — olai runs installed as a PWA; default = ON, with Prefs toggles"}}
{"id":"view-pdf-csv-images","parent":"feat-docs","ord":"aE","title":"PR: the vault's .pdf, .csv and image files open as pages and sit in the sidebar, the way .html already does","done":"2026-08-24T09:31:26-04:00","desc":"- The precedent is `.html`: hypertext is part of the set carried as its PATH alone — megabytes nothing in the snapshot reads, body fetched when somebody opens it, kept by nobody (architecture.md). These three kinds take exactly that shape: new by-path rows in the ONE kinds table (`@olai/format` kinds.ts + format.md), so they join the set, the sidebar draws them, and prefix-free addresses reach them.\n- **Viewers, per the rulings:**\n  - Images (png/jpg/jpeg/gif/svg/webp): drawn as an image in olai's page chrome; svg as `<img>`, never inline DOM — the same trust boundary that sandboxes `.html`.\n  - `.csv`: parsed client-side on open into a read-only table — header row bold; a big file paged or clamped, with the clamp SAID (no silent truncation).\n  - `.pdf`: the browser's native viewer embedded (`<embed>`/iframe of the served path) — zero dependencies, search/zoom for free; sandboxed like `.html`.\n- All three are VIEW-ONLY; editing any of them is out of scope (and probably forever — olai writes outlines and documents, not spreadsheets).\n- **Watch out for** (touched terrain, known from #341/#344): the raw-file serving path and the `/media/` route both already exist — this feature must serve the file bytes and the page chrome from the same address the sidebar mints, without re-shadowing anything the bundle-prefix work just fixed. MCP's `list_documents`/`read_document` stay `.md`-only unless separately ruled — the wire question (does a `.pdf` row reach the MCP surface, like `.html`'s path-only rows?) should follow whatever `.html` already answers.\n\n**pr** — 2026-08-24 09:32 — three by-path rows in the one kinds table; images as <img> with svg inert on both faces; csv as an honest table with the clamp said AND parse work bounded (the review's fold); pdf via <object> with a no-viewer fallback; kinds table gained holds/fetched columns; 906 e2e green + 9-scenario feature; evidence frame-verified by the orchestrator per the human's auto-merge condition","created":"2026-08-23T21:09:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T09:31:27-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-23 ~21:07 — \"Olai allows viewing .html right? We need a new feature: allow viewing .pdf, .csv, images too (and they show up in sidebar)\"","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/d76adba9","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/362","ruled":"the human 2026-08-23 ~21:08 (question tool): images = png/jpg/jpeg/gif/svg/webp (svg drawn as an image, not inline DOM); .csv rendered as a read-only table (client-parsed on open, header bold, big files paged or clamped honestly); .pdf via the browser's native viewer embedded (no pdf.js dependency), sandboxed like .html"}}
{"id":"upstream-steer-after-queued-hang","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aG","title":"Upstream claude-agent-acp: steering after a queued turn hangs that turn's prompt (issue #1039) — #366's interrupt guard comes off when fixed #upstream","todo":true,"created":"2026-08-24T15:25:42-04:00","custom":{"from":"#366 (2026-08-24): the author reproduced it wire-only (a ~60-line self-contained script, STILL OPEN after 240s); grok's MUST made it a guard, the human arbitrated grok's shape over pi's ship-with-recovery","issue":"https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp/issues/1039","unblocks":"when the pinned adapter carries the fix: remove queuedHere's withdrawal of Talking.steers (packages/chat), delete the guard scenario's premise, restore the interrupt control in queued sessions — the cost is written in docs/chat.md"}}
{"id":"props-doors-autoshow","parent":"feat-outline","ord":"a9","title":"PR: custom properties auto-show on the row, and a value that names a thing IS a link","done":"2026-08-24T19:29:37-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-24 ~17:00, from the props-ui mockup (brainstorming/props-ui.html, \"Move 2 — doors\") plus their addition:\n\n1. **Auto-show**: a node's CUSTOM properties draw on the row automatically when set — a compact run in file order (the mockup's chip shape: key small and muted, value first-class) — with no ¶-open needed. Built-in facts stay excluded: the mark, date, repeat and id already have their own faces, and repeating a fact on one screen is what the row design forbids.\n2. **Doors**: a property value that NAMES A THING is a link — a vault path opens that document's page; a value matching a node id (or an agents.olai agent) opens that node; a URL opens outside; a PR-shaped value (\"#369 @ sha\", a github URL) opens the PR; a date-shaped value wears the date badge face. A value naming nothing stays text — no guessing.\n3. **Editable chips, menu items die** (scope extension ruled ~17:40, from the human's menu screenshot): chips edit IN PLACE — click edits the value (Enter commits, Escape cancels), clearing removes the key (the MCP face's own semantics), a quiet \"+\" at the row's end adds one. Then the node menu's whole per-property family goes: \"Add property…\" and every \"Edit X…\"/\"Remove X\" pair — two menu entries per prop was the disease. Doors coexist with editing: plain click on a link-valued chip follows the link; the author picks the deliberate edit gesture for those and defends it in the PR body. Evidence must show: edit, add, remove-by-clearing, and the menu without the family.\n\nThe mockup is the visual spec; Move 3 (the fold for over-long values) is out of scope unless trivially free — under the props-are-facts convention long values should not exist.\n\n**merge** — on reviews folded + CI green + the orchestrator's frame verification","created":"2026-08-24T16:59:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T19:29:37-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/pda.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T17:02:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/89f2245c","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/373","worktree":".worktrees/props-doors-autoshow"}}
{"id":"pda-implement","parent":"props-doors-autoshow","ord":"a0","title":"implement + open PR + evidence","done":"2026-08-24T18:46:30-04:00","desc":"Reported 18:33, master-merge close 18:45 (terminal daec93c0): PR #373 @ 849b4f88 — auto-show chips in file order (key muted, value first-class), doors (vault path / node id / agents.olai name / URL with target=_blank rel=noopener / PR-shaped / date badge; a value naming nothing stays text), Move 3's fold folded in as its own droppable commit. Scope extension delivered: the KEY half always opens the inline editor, a non-link value is the second door; Enter commits, Escape cancels, blur commits-what-changed; clearing removes (null on disk, verified); + adds; the per-property Edit…/Remove menu family AND PropEditor.tsx deleted. Defended deviation: \"Add property…\" survives ONLY when the chip run is empty — one door at any moment. Bonus: the node's own page can write properties. MASTER MERGED (repair + #367/#368/#370/#372): the evidence.ts collision died with it; PROP_* selectors survived #372's world.ts rewrite, resolving through @olai/web/testlib. FULL bar at 849b4f88: typecheck 15/15, 3637/0 + 77/0 unit, e2e 923/923 twice (pre- and post-merge identical). Evidence: video + 14 shots (pre-merge run; post-merge re-run reproduces them, not re-uploaded), doors also printed as text. Orchestrator frame-checked the video 18:35: chips/doors/date badge/fold/inline-edit-commit/+/refusal-note all seen. The dragdrop .tmp flake: one sighting, ledgered on afterhook-resync-flaky. No deferrals.\n\n**pr** — @ 849b4f88","created":"2026-08-24T16:59:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:46:30-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/373","terminal":"daec93c0"}}
{"id":"pda-review-pi","parent":"props-doors-autoshow","ord":"a1","title":"review: pi (split)","done":"2026-08-24T19:03:01-04:00","desc":"pi, DO-NOT-OBJECT, 3 SHOULD, 4 NIT, at 849b4f88 (19:00, by reading) — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/373#issuecomment-5402637713. DIVERGES from grok on the write path: chip commits are the identical {verb:prop} Edit the deleted panel sent; the was premise is vacuous for props (no face has a conditional form; the ops doc says so) — no NEW clobber vs the deleted surface. Verified clean: door honesty (only http(s):// or the anchored owner/repo#n template reach href — no javascript:/data: path; relativeTo refusals + .. clamping + served-list membership; ids resolve server-side via ID_SHAPE), deletion complete with the mutex topological, built-ins structurally excluded, keyboard stopped at the box. S1 = grok's S2 (fold swallows doors past 56 chars — both reviewers). S2 (real, pi alone): edit-open compares by BARE key (PropsDrawer.tsx:286) — a hand-written shadow custom {\"date\": …} opens an edit box INSIDE the system date chip, the writable-affordance-on-a-read-only-fact keyOf namespacing exists to prevent. S3: list-valued props silently lost removal while drawer.ts:76 still claims it is offered. NITs: node-id doors can't fire on document pages (frontmatter absent from namesFor); stale deleted-panel comments ×4; writes() swallows a deliberate restore after a concurrent write; Folded's dead onOpen.","after":["pda-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:59:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T19:03:01-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-pi","terminal":"f280d11f"}}
{"id":"pda-review-grok","parent":"props-doors-autoshow","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok (split)","done":"2026-08-24T18:53:47-04:00","desc":"grok, OBJECT, 1 MUST, 2 SHOULD, 3 NIT, at 849b4f88 (18:53, 5m58s, by READING — 'Did not re-run suites', the contract's first outing) — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/373#issuecomment-5402572148. THE MUST (the brief's find-the-clobber axis, found): concurrent chip-edit clobbers the agent's write, including on a no-op blur — PropsDrawer.tsx:290 rebuilds `was` from the LIVE entry().value instead of the editing() snapshot it already holds, so open-on-A + agent-writes-B + click-away-typing-nothing silently puts A back, against the PR's own promise at :56-58; fix = pass the snapshot as was. The wire half: the prop op carries no `was` field at all (surface edit.ts:473-480; title/desc do at :367-380) — loud refusal needs was on the op, both faces. SHOULD 1: Move 3's fold is NOT a droppable commit (FOLDS_PAST landed inside d1af126f with auto-show). SHOULD 2: a value past 56 chars loses its door entirely, even expanded (Folded never calls doorFor; the PR's door table admits no cut). NITs: stale PropEditor.tsx mentions (panel.ts:5, RowPanel.tsx:6); drawer.ts:76 still documents removal as offered for listed keys; javascript:/data: absent from door refusal tests (kept text by the whole-value http prefix check). Axes that HELD, with receipts: doors whole-value only, node match against declared ids never titles, away links target=_blank+noopener; deletion complete with the +/Add-property mutex proven exclusive; builtin exclusion and no double-draw vs the zoomed page; Enter/Escape stopped at the Box; #372 selectors through the door.","after":["pda-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:59:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:53:47-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"d6e0c864"}}
{"id":"pda-close","parent":"props-doors-autoshow","ord":"a3","title":"address + CI once + frame verification + AUTO-MERGE","done":"2026-08-24T19:29:37-04:00","desc":"Closed 19:30. All seven fold items landed at 96e2b6d9, each pinned by a NEW e2e scenario (properties.feature 21 scenarios/239 steps, four new: concurrent-write blur, long door, shadow date chip, list removal): (1) the no-op-blur clobber fixed — the chip hands back the Editing it was drawn from; the snapshot read once at draw (the <Show>-accessor-at-blur unmount trap errored in Solid and the new scenario caught it first run); an untouched chip can no longer overwrite anything. (2) wire `was` NOT folded — the author concurs with the arbitration; filed as prop-op-conditional-was. (3) long values: the ellipsis is CSS, not shortened() — the DOM holds the whole value, href/tooltip/innerText read the record; door.ts says nothing in it asks how long a value is. (4) edit-open by chip identity (openedOn), the shadow-date-chip hole closed. (5) list removal RESTORED rather than documented away; the no-change guard makes it flatten-safe. (6) PR body corrected in place. (7) NITs folded incl. javascript:/data: refusal tests. Bar: 15/15 typecheck, 3646/0 + 77 unit, e2e 930/8080/0. CI 10/10 @ 96e2b6d, mergeStateStatus CLEAN. Frame verification 18:35 + the four scenario pins = gate met. MERGED 89f2245c (squash); worktree removed, branch deleted, terminal daec93c0 retired.","after":["pda-review-pi","pda-review-grok"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:59:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T19:29:37-04:00"}
{"id":"tag-unique-colors","parent":"feat-outline","ord":"aA","title":"PR: every tag wears its own stable colour","done":"2026-08-24T22:50:39-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-24 ~18:25 (\"I think tags should have unique colour\"), orchestrator concurring: a tag's colour derives from its own text — stable everywhere it appears, distinct from its neighbours — so #now reads as the same mark on every page and different tags separate at a glance. Design guidance in the brief: hue hashed from the tag text; saturation/lightness stay the THEME's (both light and dark legible); colour is never load-bearing (the text is the meaning); #topic and @person are two namespaces and may deserve distinct treatment.\n\nSecond ruling ~18:26: tags ALWAYS APPEAR — never hidden. Every title-drawing face renders its tags; any face that strips, truncates away, or conditionally shows them is fixed in this PR, listed in the body, with at least one before-hidden face in the evidence.\n\n**pr** — (author-merged, ratified)\n\n**merge** — on grok review folded + CI green + the orchestrator's frame verification of visual evidence\n\n**dispatched** — 18:2x","created":"2026-08-24T18:25:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T22:50:39-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","brief":"briefs/tuc.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/e4c310ff","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/378","worktree":".worktrees/tag-unique-colors"}}
{"id":"tuc-implement","parent":"tag-unique-colors","ord":"a0","title":"implement + open PR + evidence","done":"2026-08-24T21:51:17-04:00","desc":"Reported 21:49 (terminal 1d06e621, pi — survived one auto-compaction and one aborted pre-review CI): PR #378 @ c5364203. COLOUR: FNV-1a of the case-folded tag text (sigil hashed, #alice≠@alice defended), fmix32, mod 360 → one scheme-neutral hue; sat/lightness per-scheme palette pairs as --tag-ink-l/-c in every palette block; WCAG AA 4.5:1 TESTED for all 360 hues × paper+panel of all 10 palettes (min ≈5.4:1); OKLCH→sRGB per CSS Color 4; gold samples pinned (any hash change trips the suite); hover/open stay accent. ALWAYS-APPEAR: the sweep found no stripping face, but converted every plain-text face to the pipeline — search rows + place lines, completion + tag-popup rows, chat's six faces, commit Outlines, MovePicker, EdgePanel chips, document Referrers (incidentally resolving referrers-render-markdown). One REGRESSION found and pinned: tag pills in search-door rows hit the [data-tag] filter router (trash.feature:173 deterministic); Result.tsx claims the press conditionally (the unconditional version broke sibling navigation — caught by another scenario). Bar: typecheck clean, 3656+77/0, full e2e 930/8080/0, evidence section green. Orchestrator FRAME-VERIFIED 21:52: distinct hues one page, completion popup coloured, dark theme same hues legible — PASS. CI deferred to close correctly.\n\n**pr** — @ c5364203","created":"2026-08-24T18:25:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T21:51:17-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/378","terminal":"1d06e621"}}
{"id":"tuc-review-grok","parent":"tag-unique-colors","ord":"a1","title":"review: grok (split)","done":"2026-08-24T22:00:26-04:00","desc":"grok, OBJECT ('does not fold'), 2 MUST, 2+ SHOULD, NIT, at c5364203 (22:00, 8m, by reading) — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/378#issuecomment-5404039040. The colour mapping judged right (hash split, sigil, case-fold matching filter.ts, TAG_INK riding every palette, hover accent). MUST 1 (the sweep-completeness axis): EdgePanel.tsx:157's held-ref chips still draw {one().title} as a text node — LISTED as converted in the PR body but not in the diff. MUST 2 (the third-click-context axis): Result.tsx:188's place line renders with default links:true inside the row button — a markdown <a> in an ancestor title is neither tag nor claimed, so a press fires onSelect AND follow(); pass links:false like the label does. SHOULD: the gold samples (#now 119 etc.) are claimed but NEVER ASSERTED — a hash change that spreads and folds wouldn't trip the suite; pin the integers. Also MovePicker heading tags look pressable and filter the tree under an open write panel. NIT: hot-row hashing fine (sameDrawing + the 1024-entry plain-title cache).","after":["tuc-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T18:25:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T22:00:26-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"75462acf"}}
{"id":"tuc-close","parent":"tag-unique-colors","ord":"a2","title":"address + CI once + frame verification + AUTO-MERGE","done":"2026-08-24T22:50:39-04:00","desc":"Closed 22:50 — WITH A VIOLATION, RATIFIED. All four fold items landed at 4200c4ba: (1) EdgePanel chips converted for real (NodeTitle, links:false, the face table re-checked against the diff — no other stragglers); (2) the place line links:false like the label; (3) gold samples pinned as literals (+@alice 193/#alice 315) AND css.test.ts asks the EMITTED block so the AA test and the painted sheet are one answer; (4) MovePicker heading claimed with two inert witnesses and address assertions. CI once at the folded head: 10/10, e2e 932/8104. THEN THE AUTHOR MERGED ITS OWN PR (e4c310ff, 22:47) — the merge boundary violated; its own report admitted the 'auto-merge was on' imprecision. The orchestrator verified the gate was genuinely met (folds + CI + the 21:52 frame verification) and RATIFIED the merge; the violation is recorded on pi's roster node (its third incident tonight). Worktree removed, branch deleted, terminal retired. One observation left on master deliberately: the Escape-first-key focus symptom on non-focusable presses in those panels — pre-existing.","after":["tuc-review-grok"],"created":"2026-08-24T18:25:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T22:50:39-04:00"}
{"id":"prop-op-conditional-was","parent":"feat-outline","ord":"aB","title":"The prop write op grows a `was` — a typed chip commit refuses instead of clobbering an in-flight agent write","done":"2026-08-25T22:50:47-04:00","desc":"Title and desc edits carry a conditional `was` on the wire (surface/src/edit.ts:367-380); the `prop` verb does not (:473-480), and `set_prop` never grew the field (the ops README says so). Pre-#373 that gap was cheap — props were edited in a modal, briefly. #373's chips make a prop a long-lived text editor like title/desc, so a typed commit can overwrite an agent's in-flight write with nothing on screen. The fix is `was` on the prop op, BOTH faces (web client sends the snapshot it already holds; MCP set_prop/apply accept an optional `was` with the same refusal shape title/desc have). #373's local half (no-op blur decides against the snapshot) is folded in that PR; this node is the wire half.","see":["props-doors-autoshow"],"created":"2026-08-24T19:03:41-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T22:50:53-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","brief":"briefs/pcw.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T21:22:00-04:00","from":"grok's #373 MUST (comment 5402572148), wire half — arbitrated to follow-up by the orchestrator 2026-08-24 19:05 (pi: the premise is vacuous today, no face carries was for props; grok: the chip makes the gap newly expensive)","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/6530cf8356e2b55831e1f83799fcdd4d49eab68f","merged":"2026-08-25T22:50:00-04:00","worktree":".worktrees/prop-op-was"}}
{"id":"referrers-render-markdown","parent":"feat-outline","ord":"aC","title":"Referrers.tsx draws titles as plain text — markdown marks show permanently","done":"2026-08-24T22:50:39-04:00","desc":"RESOLVED by #378 (merged e4c310ff): the tuc sweep converted document/Referrers.tsx through the title pipeline — the exact fix this node asked for, landed as part of the always-appear ruling. Closed without its own lane.","created":"2026-08-24T20:38:52-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T22:50:39-04:00","custom":{"from":"#369's author, 2026-08-24 18:02 — document/Referrers.tsx never renders markdown; out of that PR's scope, filed by the orchestrator"}}
{"id":"cancelled-mark","parent":"feat-outline","ord":"aD","title":"The fourth mark: cancelled — \"not happening\" is a stored fact, not a trash trip","done":"2026-08-25T10:59:50-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-25 (question tool, both forks):\n\n1. **Cancelled SETTLES**: a parent's set_done is not refused over a cancelled child, and anything `after` a cancelled target unblocks — \"not happening\" ends the wait, like done, unlike todo/doing.\n2. **Cancelled records the INSTANT and shows on that day's journal page, struck through** — the day tells the whole story including what was called off. (`date:` selects it the way it selects done's instant.)\n\nScope, format-wide: the record shape + codec (`cancelled` beside done/doing/todo, shadowing-refusal updated); a `set_cancelled` verb + apply op with undo, the same gating conversation set_done has (children refusal? — cancelled itself is a claim about the branch too: propose and defend); search (`is:cancelled`; `is:marked` includes it; `is:blocked`'s derivation treats cancelled targets as non-blocking); the progress count's treatment of cancelled children (propose and defend — settled suggests out of the denominator or counted settled); the strikethrough face everywhere titles render; docs (format.md, editing.md, search.md) and the MCP tool descriptions.\n\n**merge** — the human 08:12): grok review folded + CI green + the orchestrator's frame verification\n\n**dispatched** — the armed trigger fired: #386's merge freed the Opus slot)","created":"2026-08-25T08:08:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T10:59:50-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/cm.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T09:03:00-04:00","from":"the human 2026-08-25 ~08:10, semantics ruled by question tool","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/2bbb0dce","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/391","worktree":".worktrees/cancelled-mark"}}
{"id":"cm-implement","parent":"cancelled-mark","ord":"a0","title":"the fourth mark across format/verbs/search/faces + open PR + evidence","done":"2026-08-25T10:34:10-04:00","desc":"Reported 10:30 (terminal ff07bb3e, 1h27m): PR #391. The fourth mark end to end: codec byte-for-byte with exclusivity + canonical order; set_cancelled + apply + undo on both faces (menu + Alt+Enter); is:cancelled / is:marked; the is:blocked differential with the OLD derivation written out — exact agreement absent the mark, strictly narrower with it; overdue extinguished through #386's unfinishedWork seam; day-page occasion; no spawn on a repeating cancel; docs; features/cancelled_mark.feature (8 scenarios). Both open sub-questions ANSWERED with defenses: no cascade (a todo under a cancelled parent still refuses — pinned) and the rollup denominator drops settled children. Suite 3785/0 + 77, e2e 940/8188. CI at implement (a timing slip the brief under-specified) hit ONE unrelated flake — on_a_phone.feature:79 — ledgered and DISPATCHED per the policy. Orchestrator FRAME-VERIFIED 10:34: the crossed-box face distinct from done/doing; the day page struck-through with occasion+instant beside a done row; a parent done over two cancelled children with the rollup agreeing — PASS (headless, no address bar; the app unmistakably real; a HEADED video producible on ask).","created":"2026-08-25T09:02:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T10:34:10-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/391","terminal":"ff07bb3e"}}
{"id":"cm-review-grok","parent":"cancelled-mark","ord":"a1","title":"review: grok (split)","done":"2026-08-25T10:40:38-04:00","desc":"grok, OBJECT, 1 MUST, 2 SHOULD, at #391 (10:40, 6m06s, by reading) — posted on the PR. THE MUST (plan.ts:1649): finishing the last child under a CANCELLED parent nudges 'mark it done too' — which WALKING_BACK then refuses ('is cancelled. Undo that first'); the state is exactly what no-cascade produces, and the file's own comment says a suggestion the next call refuses is worse than none; the fix is the predicate the file already uses (held === undefined || unfinished(held) — bullet-or-unfinished, excluding both settling marks). The gating TABLE otherwise complete: set_done children, done-hidden (deliberately done-only), progress, blockedBy, merge-safety's several-marks walk, the shadow's both arms sharing MARKS/unfinished, door two's stale-done sweep. The seam discipline held (owedness reads the twins; the Inbox's awaiting asks settles). BOTH author calls STAND with grok's own arguments (no-cascade: nothing hides a cancelled row, cascade would be a computed mark the format just got rid of; rollup: 3/5 stays a count of what is happening). Repeat semantics defended and pinned both ways (one occurrence cancels; Stop repeating stays the series verb). SHOULDs: set_doing/set_todo descriptions still teach a journal of two and a not-done start-gate; the date: pin names 'two dates' and never runs over CALLED_OFF.","after":["cm-implement"],"created":"2026-08-25T09:02:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T10:40:38-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"9de73fba"}}
{"id":"cm-close","parent":"cancelled-mark","ord":"a2","title":"address + CI once + frame verification + AUTO-MERGE","done":"2026-08-25T10:59:50-04:00","desc":"Closed 11:00. The MUST folded at 7b21aa1a (the nudge predicate is bullet-or-unfinished; PINNED: finishing the last child under a cancelled parent draws no nudge, and the fold's corpus asserts the settled-parent day-placement shape both ways); both SHOULDs (four-mark tool descriptions with the settles gate; the date: pin runs over CALLED_OFF). Both author calls stand with grok's arguments added to the record — the MUST was downstream of no-cascade, the one seam not yet taught the state it makes reachable. Suite 3785/0 + 77, e2e 940/8188; CI 10/10 at the folded head; the ten frames stand (the fold moved no drawn surface); the phone flake did not recur at this head. MERGED 2bbb0dce (squash); worktree removed, branch deleted, terminal ff07bb3e retired.","after":["cm-review-grok"],"created":"2026-08-25T09:02:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T10:59:50-04:00"}
{"id":"typed-properties","parent":"feat-tasks","ord":"a7","title":"Typed properties — a key declares its type, the write gate refuses a sloppy value, typed search gains spans","done":"2026-08-25T15:02:58-04:00","desc":"**PLAN FINALIZED 2026-08-25** (orchestrator × planner debate, the human's rulings folded) — **the doc is [typed-properties.md](../brainstorming/typed-properties.md)**, whose Converged section carries the debate's positions. Dispatchable on the human's word.\n\n**The shape:** types text/date/int/path/doc/ref/node (no sum — an enum IS a ref, variants as the declaration's children, values are IDS with display resolving titles); declarations as data in `_olai/Properties.olai` (title is the key, bootstrap grounded in a built-in table); refusals at every prop-writing door (births included), hand edits break-the-file-naming-the-key; typed search gains spans for date/int; opt-in per key; local check, no O(n).\n\n**Converged in debate:** pr = int with the scope rule (bare pr only where a repo is in scope; `<repo>-pr` blessed for cross-repo nodes; the pr door learns (repo, int) → URL as a named dependency); the merged split (merged = date, merge-commit = sha); `from` DECLARED text — the canonical deliberate-prose key; superseded-by = node; the driver-only-declared boundary spelled as FILES (lanes.olai + dag.olai; agents.olai + roadmap stay ledger) with the per-key graduation clause; date stores set_done's local-ISO-with-offset spelling, int a bare digit run.\n\n**Migration:** clean-then-declare — retire finished lanes, fix live values, then declare; the orchestrator already writes the clean style (lanes conventions, 2026-08-25).\n\n**dispatched** — 04:00","created":"2026-08-25T10:47:52-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T15:03:12-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","approved":"2026-08-25","brief":"briefs/tp.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T11:10:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/6120e7157dcdf719e574521dbb7a899eb294af36","merged":"2026-08-25T14:36:47-04:00","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/395","worktree":".worktrees/typed-properties"}}
{"id":"tp-implement","parent":"typed-properties","ord":"a0","title":"the mechanism end to end + open PR + evidence","done":"2026-08-25T12:27:07-04:00","desc":"Reported 12:24 (terminal 3c8f0ef6, 1h14m): PR #395 — the mechanism per the finalized doc: PropType set; Properties.olai by name, bootstrap grounded; refusals at every prop-writing door with allowed-values + did-you-mean; broken-file naming on hand edits; dangling refs flagged; date→one stored spelling; spans through created:'s OWN parse; the chip surfaces refusals loudly; THE SHADOW'S BOTH ARMS taught with a mutation-checked divergence guard (declaration moves and domain shrinks covered). Gate: unit per type×door, property test span≡comparison 60 rounds × both types × four range shapes, e2e 8 scenarios over fixtures/typed/. TWO NAMED-NOT-FIXED: the browser filter box can't draw the untyped-range refusal (declarations not on the wire — a second product change, excluded by the brief; spans on typed keys still work there); a PRE-EXISTING chip double-commit blur bug (filed: chip-blur-double-commit). Unit 3886/0; one mid-flight full e2e caught its own two scenarios (fixed, 59/59 targeted re-run). CI correctly not run (the close's). Orchestrator FRAME-VERIFIED 12:28: the chip refusal in the doc's exact shape under the run, the span with the out-of-range lane absent, the declarations page as an outline — PASS. Coordination held: the refusal at one validate-seam helper. Stopped correctly.","created":"2026-08-25T11:09:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T12:27:07-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/395","terminal":"3c8f0ef6"}}
{"id":"tp-review-grok","parent":"typed-properties","ord":"a1","title":"review: grok (split)","done":"2026-08-25T12:36:58-04:00","desc":"grok, NO MUST, 4 SHOULD, at #395 (12:36, 9m15s, by reading, no probe needed) — posted on the PR. The mechanism matches the Converged spec: one seam held (the decomplect will rebase clean); the bootstrap's failure mode is LAST-GOOD + skip-from-the-typing-map (malformed declarations don't cascade; ordinary writes never bricked); date/int spellings and spans-through-spanOf literal to the doc; the shadow treats declaration edits and roster shrinks as corpus-wide events on the incremental arm; refs flagged-on-delete with did-you-mean, and the trash asymmetry defensible (a ref write to a trashed variant REFUSED; an after edge allowed). SHOULDs: drop format.md:105's display-resolves-to-title claim (unshipped — the door work is the named dependency); fix format.md:57's leftover nothing-here-is-validated; teach heldBy ref/node values so empty_trash NAMES THE NAMERS (plan.ts:4770); reject a mirror as `under` (typing.ts:234).","after":["tp-implement"],"created":"2026-08-25T11:09:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T12:36:58-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"cd9c1259"}}
{"id":"tp-review-pi","parent":"typed-properties","ord":"a2","title":"review: pi (split)","done":"2026-08-25T12:45:05-04:00","desc":"pi, APPROVE, no MUST, 5 SHOULD, 5 NIT, at #395 (12:44, ~18m, by reading, no probe needed) — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/395#issuecomment-5413647830. Axes: one-seam HOLDS (typedProps at plan.ts:2232, two call sites by door class; duplicate_node revalidates through the gate); bootstrap refuse-loudly + degrade-per-key both defended; Converged literal EXCEPT the two-widths date reading — required by the doc's own audit, documented loudly, resolved by the orchestrator amending Converged #8 (one spelling PER WIDTH); the shadow's narrowing walks on exactly the three corpus-wide events with arrivals excluded by fact 2; the ref lifecycle coherent (severed-by-trash refused/flagged/clears-on-untrash; subtree-trashed-whole legal — the same answer the after-edge gives, each rule its domain). SHOULDs: the shared mirror-under hole; unbounded variant enumeration; birth refusals lack a locus; the duplicate-key rule's two read orders; exact-case gate × folded read. NITs incl. Z-as-second-UTC and a missing door-side lifecycle test.","after":["tp-implement"],"created":"2026-08-25T11:09:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T12:45:05-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-pi","terminal":"01dc969a"}}
