{"id":"terminal-door","parent":"orch-kolu","ord":"a4","title":"The terminal door (#405)","doing":true,"desc":"The human's ask (2026-08-25): \"I keep checking the kolu Dock for terminal/agent status — reflect it in olai itself.\" The answer: put the status where the fact already is — the `terminal` property becomes a DOOR.\n\n- **Rung 1, the dot** — the chip wears the agent's bucket: green working, amber pulsing awaiting, gray parked, hollow-with-words when padi is absent. Rides one standing mirror of padi's `terminals` collection (ten tabs = one connection; kolu pushes deltas, nothing polls).\n- **Rung 2, the snapshot** — click → the card grows a `screen.text` pane (dashed border, \"snapshot · just now\", refetch, open-in-kolu). One verb per click, nothing subscribed.\n- Because the door hangs off the PROPERTY, it lights up in the plain outline view of lanes.olai the day it merges — no new route needed, so this ships BEFORE the /orchestrator page and is the phase plan's first visible payoff.\n- Scope: the padi mirror (`cells.kolu`, `collections.fleet` + owner overlay), `procedures.screen`, the chip renderer keyed on the prop KEY (`terminal`). Migrates to keying off the declared type when someone orders it — a rename-sized diff, deliberately not a dependency.\n- Consumes kolu#2216 (`@kolu/padi-client`) UNMERGED at its pinned head by the human's ruling — the first out-of-repo consumer validates the contract; two gaps + one residual found and amended pre-merge (the flow working as designed).\n- **RULED 2026-08-25 ~21:45 (the human): the padi-facing kit is `@olai/kolu-client`, its own package** — the wall makes the dependency direction physics (kolu-client can never cyclically depend back on server; a directory permits that entanglement one import at a time). \"Second consumer\" is NOT a graduation requirement — the anti-cycle enforcement alone earns the wall when the code is already leafward-only. The author's earlier `packages/orchestrator` died on its NAME (domain noun for functional code) and dashboard framing, not on package-hood.\n- Visual: the Terminal Door artifact (interactive ladder mock, reef/aurora, 2026-08-25) — to be checked into brainstorming/ when the UI settles.\n- **Folded in mid-lane (the human, 2026-08-26, during the live test): the padi connection's status joins the header bar beside \"live\"** — connected / absent / contract-skew as a small indicator drawing from the same `cells.kolu` the dots consume (a second reader of the existing cell, no new wire). Rationale: a per-chip hollow face is ambiguous (unknown terminal? dead mirror?) — app health belongs in app chrome, and skew's \"upgrade one of these\" sentence is header-grade. (Briefly its own node `padi-status-header`; trashed 2026-08-26 as redundant — same PR, the human's call.)\n- **Lane state (stage children folded away 2026-08-26)**: reviews grok APPROVE (2/2) + pi's MUST/SHOULDs discharged and folded; one CI run green (11/11 incl. CodeQL, 0 alerts) at the pre-dock-row head; deployed unmerged and live-verified twice. Merge order: #2216 first (merged 35732510) → re-pin → this.\n- **THE PR IS NOT DONE (the human, 2026-08-26): it stays open to absorb the dock-row fold** (child `dock-row`) — kolu's Dock row replacing the inline dot outright, the ratified deletions, the attention-feed mirror. It merges only when EVERYTHING the human asked for is in, re-CI'd once at the final head, live-verified, and the human gives the word. cb9dcd13 lives as author through all of it.","created":"2026-08-25T16:53:39-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T11:58:48-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/td.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T19:00:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/405","terminal":"cb9dcd13","worktree":".worktrees/terminal-door"}}
{"id":"terminal-stream","parent":"feat-orch","ord":"aB","title":"PR: the terminal streams — the snapshot pane goes live while held open (orchestrator phase 6)","todo":true,"desc":"Rung 3 of the terminal door — the \"someday\" (terminals streamed into olai) graduated to a phase, 2026-08-25.\n\n- The expanded pane goes live: padi's existing `terminalAttach`, relayed through olai's surface as a scoped, REFCOUNTED stream member — two tabs on the same terminal share one attach; the last close detaches and padi stops emitting. Attach only while visible: twelve lanes = twelve dots and at most one stream.\n- xterm hosts the pane; frames get the chat panel's treatment (throttled cadence, appends). Solid border + \"● live\" tag vs the snapshot's dashed border — the pane says which promise it is making.\n- READ-ONLY: typing into the terminal stays kolu's job (sendInput belongs to the driver and the chat agent, not this pane).\n- **Check before starting** (the one risk): olai's surface needs a PER-KEY stream — attach to one terminal id, not a broadcast. If `@kolu/surface`'s stream members can't scope by key, that's a small upstream ask to file first, not to discover mid-PR.\n- Anytime after terminal-door; independent of phases 2-5.","after":["terminal-door"],"created":"2026-08-25T16:53:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T10:43:02-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-p0-thin-client","parent":"orch-kolu","ord":"a2","title":"kolu: the thin padi client package #upstream","done":"2026-08-25T22:50:31-04:00","desc":"Padi's surface spec + `dial` (+ terminal-vocab schemas) as a package a consumer hydrates WITHOUT the daemon. Today olai would pull @kolu/padi whole through the npins hydrate list. Gates both 1a and 1b; `terminalAttach` comes with the spec, so the stream PR (phase 6) needs no further kolu ask.","created":"2026-08-25T16:56:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T10:40:41-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","approved":"2026-08-25","brief":"briefs/ptc.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T17:02:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/commit/35732510972024eaa9671605c3d17e1aa61bb9b2","merged":"2026-08-25T22:52:00-04:00","repo":"repo-kolu","worktree":"~/code/kolu/.worktrees/padi-thin-client"}}
{"id":"orch-p1b-page","parent":"feat-orch","ord":"a6","title":"PR: /orchestrator, read-only (phase 1b)","todo":true,"desc":"`cells.board`, `cells.needsYou`, the page, `--padi-socket`, \"no kolu\" drawn honestly. Inherits the terminal door for free — cards draw the same chip. 1a and 1b land in either order (both wait only on the thin client); door-first pays off sooner.","after":["orch-p0-thin-client"],"created":"2026-08-25T16:56:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T10:42:46-04:00"}
