{"id":"meaning-socket","parent":"feat-outline","ord":"aE","title":"PR: the meaning socket — one resolution answers \"what does this value name\", the tab receives a doors table","done":"2026-08-25T22:06:42-04:00","desc":"One module in `@olai/format` beside the validator answers \"what does a declared property value name\" — `wrongValue`/`wrongDoc`'s authority and `door.ts`'s five guesses become two arms of one consult. The browser receives ANSWERS: a per-page doors table beside `names` (the `namesFor` projection pattern — computed by the standing views once per revision, shipped on the existing page pulse; declarations STAY off the wire, preserving #395's deliberate exclusion). `door.ts` thins to answer→Route. The basis amendment: `doc`/`path` declarations gain a `base` fact (`root` | `file`) on the key's own row — gate and display read the same row; the markdown `doc` FIELD keeps beside-writer as its only premise. Kills the `typed-chips-doors` family whole (dead brief chips, raw-id ref faces, declaration-blind doors). Undeclared keys keep today's shape-guessing (errs toward no-door, the module's founding rule).","see":["typed-chips-doors"],"created":"2026-08-25T18:58:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T22:06:47-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/ms.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T20:35:00-04:00","from":"the 2026-08-25 lowy-electricity debate (finding 1, ratified) — brainstorm: lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-25.md","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/732da41968478d257f2fd33e40faff7e5e21325d","merged":"2026-08-25T22:07:00-04:00","worktree":".worktrees/meaning-socket"}}
