{"id":"terminal-door-polish","parent":"orch-kolu","ord":"a6","title":"Terminal door polish","todo":true,"desc":"Three parts filed from the human's first live session with #405 (2026-08-26); parts 2 and 3 have since been superseded.\n\n1. **The pane's default face is the themed screenshot** (the picture kolu's own `screenshot` renders — layout, box-drawing, colors, cursor preserved) — RESHAPED by pane-live: the live pane is the LOOK face; the PNG remains the candidate GLANCE face (e.g. before the pane opens, or in overviews). Measured: PNG ~1.5s/170KB incl. CLI boot. Wire: `screen.image` is on padi's surface (confirmed in the pinned contract).\n2. **SUPERSEDED → `dock-row`** (the human, 2026-08-26): the inline dot and olai's whole face vocabulary retired outright, replaced by kolu's exported Dock row. SHIPPED in #405's fold.\n3. **SUPERSEDED → `pane-live`** (the human, 2026-08-26 ~16:05): the pane live-streams via padi's `terminalAttach`; a live terminal follows its tail, so auto-scroll comes with it.","created":"2026-08-26T10:34:55-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T16:00:39-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human's first live session with #405, 2026-08-26 — the text pane's glanceability question (measured: PNG ~1.5s/170KB incl. CLI boot, near-free in-app) and the black-dot confusion (parked draws --color-muted, reading as dead; waiting deliberately folds into parked; no legend anywhere)"}}
{"id":"orch-kolu","parent":"feat-orch","ord":"a5","title":"Kolu — the padi/fleet integration family","desc":"**THE NORTH STAR (the human, 2026-08-26, on seeing the live board + ordering the live pane): \"With this, there is virtually no reason to check Kolu. I can monitor terminals in Olai itself, until I need to type something in.\"** Olai is the fleet's monitoring surface; kolu is where you go to TYPE. Every item in this family serves that sentence — and the one remaining gap it names (typing) is the actions phase (orch-p3-actions), when its day comes.","created":"2026-08-26T10:38:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T16:00:59-04:00"}
{"id":"dock-row","parent":"terminal-door","ord":"a3","title":"The Dock row export","todo":true,"desc":"One visual vocabulary: kolu ships its Dock terminal row as a package; olai's terminal face becomes it. What you see beside a node is literally what you'd see in the Dock.\n\n**The settled design (all human-ratified 2026-08-26, via the question tool):**\n- **Kolu exports the Dock row** as a package — the `@kolu/solid-statepip` precedent. The Dock itself consumes the export, so the two cannot drift. The package takes a plain prop bag; `bindStatePip` is already pure and moves as-is.\n- **Full visual row**: pip + glyph, status words, intent line, recency, repo-color stripe, sleeping recede, PR badge. Kolu-app-local bits (unread wash, ⌘N hints, active-tile highlight) become optional props olai simply doesn't set.\n- **Attention feeds mirrored now**: `@kolu/padi-client` grows the urgency cell + activity stream; `@olai/kolu-client` mirrors them; the pure feeds→attention-class fold gets exported so consumers don't restate it.\n- **Tailwind stays**: olai already runs Tailwind v4; the row keeps its utility classes + `@kolu/theme` tokens.\n- **Sequencing**: kolu PR first, HELD UNMERGED until the human's EXPLICIT approval; kolu-side CI parallel with the olai fold, never gating it.\n\n**THE FIFTH SITTING'S RATIFIED CONSTRAINT ON THE OLAI-SIDE FOLD (2026-08-26 — the fold must not be briefed without this):**\n- **Deletion, not reconciliation**: when the row lands, delete `DotFace`, `LIVE_FACES`, `DOT_FACES`, `face.ts` + `face.test.ts`, `.olai-dot`/`.olai-dot-slot`/`@keyframes olai-dot-awaiting`, `FACE_SAYS`. No `agentState` field beside `face` — one question, one answer.\n- **The wire stays olai's flat projection**: it carries what the row's prop bag declares plus `owner` (fleet.ts's law — a field crosses when something draws it); agent state as `Schema.NullOr(Schema.String)`. **No olai-declared closed set of kolu state, ever** (swept: `KoluStatus` stays — it describes olai's dial). `@olai/surface` NEVER imports `@kolu/terminal-vocab` (the literals aren't exported as an array; the import would compile the per-agent schema graph into the outline wire spec).\n- **The closed set's one home is the row package's prop bag**, which exports its own narrowing guard — the browser-side fill narrows wire strings through it, unknown states degrade visibly. The type fence stays at `rowOf`.\n- **The five-home header map rides the same fold**: cross-reference paragraphs in surface/kolu.ts, kolu-client/index.ts, server's join, the web props, chat/src/kolu.ts.\n\n**THE DISPATCH RULING (the human, on ratification): no new PRs.** The olai-side fold + deletions ride the EXISTING olai lane — #405's author cb9dcd13, on its PR — once the kolu head exists to pin. The kolu-side additions ride the in-flight dock-row-export PR (see child).\n\nSupersedes terminal-door-polish part 2 (the dot legend).","created":"2026-08-26T10:59:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T11:58:10-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human, 2026-08-26: \"Why not export the Kolu Dock UI as is as a package… This way we don't have to invent yet another shit in Olai\"","merge":"merge-human","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/405","terminal":"cb9dcd13"}}
{"id":"dock-row-kolu","parent":"dock-row","ord":"a0","title":"kolu PR: extract the row","doing":true,"desc":"The kolu-side half: `@kolu/solid-dockrow` (the statepip precedent) + `@kolu/padi-client` grows the attention feeds (urgency + activity + the pure fold). Full letter in the brief.\n\n**SCOPE GREW ON THE FIFTH SITTING'S RATIFICATION (the human, 2026-08-26 — rides THIS PR, no new PRs):** (1) the row package exports its narrowing guard; (2) leaf entries on the dial (lets olai delete the osfacts pin, its guard script, the types graft); (3) consumer tools riding the pin — the hydrate script + closure emitter, members lists become derived. Addendum in the brief; ledger at debates/kolu-maintenance-2026-08-26/conclusion.md.\n\n**TANDEM RULE (the human, ~12:05): kolu PR ready = olai pins immediately, no CI gate.** Consumer findings → amendment rounds → re-pin, repeat. CI ONCE each at the very end; the human reviews BOTH PRs manually as the pair's merge gate.\n\n**AMENDED (the human, ~13:35): /be HOLDS until the olai consumer is FULLY SATISFIED.** Priority: fold consumer findings (parked-arm first — the wire blocker), push + report each head for re-pin, iterate. Only on olai's \"satisfied\" does /be resume, then the drishti pin bump to final head, then /ci on order. (The gauntlet had run architecture ✅ + lens; paused there.)\n\n**THE DRISHTI PAIR (standing, never waived):** opened for the three added daemon-barrel exports; bumps to the final head after /be.\n\nRound 1 findings (all folded per the author's report): parked arm fails the row folds (amendment in flight); the closure emitter emitted DECLARED not IMPORTED; label/labelColor producers unexported → now through rowValues.","created":"2026-08-26T11:01:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T13:37:17-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/dock-row-kolu.md","dispatched":"2026-08-26T11:14:00-04:00","drishti-pr":"https://github.com/srid/drishti/pull/147","merge":"merge-human","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2217","terminal":"3594fbef","worktree":"kolu/.worktrees/dock-row-export"}}
{"id":"debate-kolu","parent":"orch-kolu","ord":"a7","title":"Debate: kolu code in olai (5th sitting)","done":"2026-08-26T11:52:15-04:00","desc":"The fifth three-AI sitting, RATIFIED by the human 2026-08-26 midday. Conclusion filed at [lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-26.md](../lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-26.md); turn files in the gitignored debates/kolu-maintenance-2026-08-26/.\n\nVerdict, converged and unanimous (two-seat — the kimi outage took pi and opencode, zero turns each): the integration is NOT complected where the feeling pointed — five homes composed, chat an honest twin (the human's \"can chat use kolu-client?\" = NO), the FleetTerminal projection acquitted by counted blast radius. Intertwined in exactly TWO places: (1) the visual vocabulary restatement (DotFace/face.ts/.olai-dot/FACE_SAYS — dies by DELETION with dock-row; no olai-declared closed set of kolu state ever again; the row package's prop bag is the one closed set and exports its narrowing; @olai/surface never imports @kolu/terminal-vocab), and (2) the hydrate machinery (kolu ships leaf entries + hydrate script + closure emitter; olai deletes the osfacts pin, guard script, types graft, hand-list down to seeds; npm killed on all four tests).\n\nTHE DISPATCH RULING (the human): no new PRs — both fixes ride the EXISTING lanes: kolu side on the in-flight dock-row-export PR (3594fbef), olai side on #405's lane (cb9dcd13) when the kolu head exists. Constraints written on the dock-row node.","created":"2026-08-26T11:11:23-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T11:52:23-04:00","custom":{"brief":"briefs/debate-kolu-2026-08-26.md","from":"the human, 2026-08-26: \"I feel like our Kolu integration code in Olai is still complecting/intertwined\" — conduct a hickey & lowy debate on the way kolu code is maintained in the olai codebase"}}
