{"id":"debate-kolu-pi","parent":"debate-kolu","ord":"a2","title":"seat: module boundaries (chair collapsed — kimi outage)","cancelled":"2026-08-26T11:28:24-04:00","desc":"The five homes as a Hickey Layer-2/3 exercise; chat/src/kolu.ts vs kolu-client (multiplication or honest twin); owns the blast-radius table per plausible kolu change.\n\nSEAT HISTORY: pi opened the chair, its provider died mid-read (kimi-k3 429 \"no deployments\", retries failed twice, zero turn files; terminal eca01375 benched warm at 49% context). I swapped to opus (f214e21d) — the human overrode before its brief was submitted: \"Pi failed, try opencode instead\"; opus terminal killed unused, the Opus slot freed. OPENCODE seats the chair (the fourth sitting's own precedent — this was opencode's chair on 08-19): terminal c0ea4db8, its roster `command` prop written on the human's order (the row had none since retirement). The human's fallback, ruled in advance: if opencode also fails, the sitting proceeds two-seat (fable + grok).","created":"2026-08-26T11:11:23-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T11:28:24-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","terminal":"c0ea4db8"}}
{"id":"dr-headers","parent":"dock-row","ord":"a1","title":"Five-home header map","done":"2026-08-26T12:06:24-04:00","desc":"Cross-reference paragraphs in the five kolu homes (surface/kolu.ts, kolu-client/index.ts, the server join, the web props, chat/src/kolu.ts) so a reader finds the map in the files. Needs no kolu head — cb9dcd13 briefed to write it now.","created":"2026-08-26T11:59:37-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T12:06:24-04:00"}
{"id":"dr-row","parent":"dock-row","ord":"a2","title":"The Dock row IS the terminal property (B)","done":"2026-08-26T16:05:44-04:00","desc":"Pin the kolu dock-row head; the terminal property renders the imported row exactly as kolu's Dock draws it (glyph, words, recency, intent, repo stripe, PR badge, sleeping recede). Wire: the bag's fields plus owner; agent state as NullOr(String); narrowing via the row package's exported guard; fence at rowOf.\n\n**GEOMETRY RULED (the human, 2026-08-26 ~13:17, from the three rendered choices on [#405's comment](https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/405#issuecomment-5428553287)): B — the full DockRow IS the terminal property.** The row replaces the chip outright; two lines per terminal always is accepted cost. (Physics found by the shots: DockRow is a two-line subgrid row needing a section container — it cannot sit inline in a chip run, so the inline slot was never real.)\n\n**WITH THE REFACTOR DIRECTIVE (the human, same breath — \"custom block render\", the Hickey sense): build the general seam today** — a property whose kind/key maps to a BLOCK renderer that owns its row, chip run the default; terminal→DockRow is the seam's first consumer; the TERMINAL_KEY branch generalizes into it, never gains a one-off sibling. Future properties plug the same socket without touching the drawer.","created":"2026-08-26T11:59:42-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T16:05:44-04:00"}
{"id":"dr-delete","parent":"dock-row","ord":"a3","title":"Delete the homegrown face vocabulary","done":"2026-08-26T14:17:51-04:00","desc":"DotFace, LIVE_FACES, DOT_FACES, face.ts + face.test.ts, .olai-dot / .olai-dot-slot / @keyframes olai-dot-awaiting, FACE_SAYS — all gone with dr-row. No olai-declared closed set of kolu state survives (KoluStatus stays — it describes olai's dial). @olai/surface never imports @kolu/terminal-vocab.\n\nSWEEP-GAP CAUGHT BY THE AUTHOR (cb9dcd13, 12:05 — the sitting's recurrence sweep missed it): `FleetTerminal.state` (`active|sleeping|parked`) is ALSO padi's record state as an olai-declared closed set. Ruled by the orchestrator on the ratified rule's standing authority: it dies into the bag's own fields (the author's first option) — not a plain-string ride.","after":["dr-row"],"created":"2026-08-26T11:59:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T14:17:51-04:00"}
{"id":"dr-attention","parent":"dock-row","ord":"a4","title":"Mirror the attention feeds","done":"2026-08-26T16:05:44-04:00","desc":"@olai/kolu-client mirrors padi's urgency cell + activity stream (grown in the kolu PR); the \"blocked on you\" emphasis computes exactly what kolu's Dock computes via the exported pure fold — full fidelity, the human's chosen cut.","created":"2026-08-26T11:59:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T16:05:44-04:00"}
{"id":"pane-live","parent":"terminal-door","ord":"a4","title":"The pane live-streams","done":"2026-08-26T17:40:23-04:00","desc":"Open pane = live terminal, not a stale photograph. The wire already offers it: padi's `streams.terminalAttach` — first frame the serialized-screen snapshot (+ scrollback cursor seed), then live deltas 1:1, defined re-attach on disconnect/overflow; `screen.history` for backfill.\n\nThe shape: the pane subscribes on open, drops on close. THE WALL HOLDS — the browser never dials padi: the olai server holds the terminalAttach subscription per open pane and relays through an `@olai/surface` stream member; rendering browser-side via kolu's own `@kolu/xterm-kit` (one vocabulary, again). A live terminal follows its tail, so this SUBSUMES terminal-door-polish part 3 (auto-scroll). The screenshot-default question (polish part 1) stays separate — the PNG is the glance face, the live pane is the look face.","created":"2026-08-26T16:00:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T17:40:23-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human, 2026-08-26 ~16:05: \"when user opens the terminal to look at snapshot, let's live stream it! Why not?\"","terminal":"cb9dcd13"}}
{"id":"app-title-hostname","ord":"aK","title":"App title: olai [hostname]","doing":true,"desc":"One PR: the app identifies its HOST everywhere it names itself — \"olai [$hostname]\" in (1) the browser tab title (document.title, including any dynamic title composition), (2) the application header chrome, (3) the PWA manifest (name/short_name so the installed app carries it). The hostname is the SERVER's (a browser cannot know it) — it crosses on the wire/config the way other server facts already do. A person running olai on two machines can tell the tabs apart; that is the whole point.","created":"2026-08-26T17:48:56-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T18:45:40-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","brief":"briefs/app-title-hostname.md","dispatched":"2026-08-26T17:58:00-04:00","from":"the human, 2026-08-26 ~17:55: the app title today is \"olai\", but it should instead be \"olai [$hostname]\" — in pwa, browser tab title, application header","merge":"merge-auto","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/410","terminal":"d6263a84","worktree":".worktrees/app-title-hostname"}}
